Deconstructing the “Free” in Free Spins
Let’s be blunt. The word “free” in this context is a legal fiction. It’s a hook. The casino is not a charity; it’s a business with a ~3-5% house edge baked into every spin. The “free” spins are a customer acquisition cost, a way to get you through the virtual door and, more importantly, to get your credit card details on file. The real transaction begins after the last free spin is used. The goal is conversion: turning a bonus hunter into a depositing, loyal player. Understanding this dynamic is the first step to not being a mark.
