Game weighting complicates the math further. Not all games contribute equally to clearing a wagering requirement. Slots typically count 100%, but table games like blackjack or roulette might only count 10-20%, and some live dealer games might not count at all. This is by design. The casino wants you playing the games with the highest house edge and the fastest turnover rate. A 100-spin package on a slot with a 96% Return to Player (RTP) is a different proposition than one on a slot with a 94% RTP. The lower the RTP, the faster your bonus balance will be eroded by the house edge during playthrough. It’s a game of attrition, and the terms are the battlefield.
