How Do Free Spins Differ from Bonus Cash?
Free spins and bonus cash are two sides of the same coin, but the psychology and mechanics differ. Free spins are a constrained experience. You get a set number of plays on a specific game, at a fixed stake. This removes player choice and focuses the excitement on a single outcome. Bonus cash, on the other hand, gives you a balance to use across the casino’s library (often with game restrictions). It feels more like “real money” and offers more autonomy. From a pure math perspective, the value is determined by the same factors: wagering requirements, game weighting, and max cashout. A €100 bonus cash offer with a 40x requirement is theoretically equivalent to a package of 1,000 free spins (valued at €0.10 each) on a 96% RTP slot with the same 40x requirement on winnings. The difference is in the player’s perception and the casino’s desired behavior—spins encourage slot play, while cash can be used to explore the lobby.
