Immediate steps include using the casino’s self-exclusion tool to block access to your account for a set period (6 months, 1 year, 5 years, or permanently). Then, contact a professional support service. In the UK, GamCare offers free, confidential advice. In the US, the National Council on Problem Gambling has a 24/7 helpline. Internationally, Gambling Therapy provides online support. These services are staffed by trained counselors who understand the psychology of addiction. Admitting you have a problem is the hardest and most important step. The casino’s “free spins” are not worth your mental health or financial stability. The house always has an edge, but you have the power to walk away from the table.
Critera for Choosing a Casino: Beyond the Bonus Banner
