Based in Hinckley, The Machine Shop was created to give people access to professional-grade tools, machinery and practical skills, whether they are complete beginners or experienced engineers. Alongside running the workshop, Bob delivers welding, machining and fabrication training, helping a new generation discover the satisfaction of building, repairing and creating with their own hands.
Through his cross pollination YouTube strategy, Bob has amassed 248,000,000 views on his work in the last 2 years. Building a substantial audience by documenting real-world engineering challenges, restoration projects and specialist fabrication work. His content showcases the process behind the repair rather than just the finished result, earning a loyal following of automotive enthusiasts, tradespeople and aspiring engineers. From hand-building components for hypercars to solving problems others consider impossible, Bob’s work combines education, entertainment and genuine craftsmanship.
Passionate about preserving practical skills and making engineering more accessible, Bob continues to champion hands-on learning through both his workshop and digital platforms. His authentic approach, technical expertise and ability to make complex engineering relatable have established him as one of the most recognisable figures in the UK’s maker and fabrication community.

