Kodiak Island Borough Housing Needs Assessment
Kodiak Island Housing Authority (KIHA) contracted with McKinley Research to conduct a Kodiak Island Borough Housing Needs Assessment. This study is intended to serve as a community resource that highlights housing needs and housing-related impacts on employment and the local economy. The report includes analysis of housing inventory, condition, and valuation; population and household demographics; community economic conditions; surveys of Kodiak road system and village housing needs; and a review of available land and zoning. This information was used to inform a housing gap analysis identifying areas of concern and unmet housing needs.

