Concierge Auctions tops $350M in bids at Hong Kong global sale
Concierge Auctions says its annual Hong Kong Global Sale drew buyers from four continents and 15 U.S. states, generating more than US$350 million in aggregate bids for luxury properties across North America and Europe. Several properties sold during the event, and the company is now accepting consignments for upcoming London and year-end auctions.
Why it matters: - The Hong Kong Global Sale showed continued demand for trophy homes even as buyers competed across borders and time zones. - Concierge Auctions used the event to showcase its global reach, digital bidding platform, and ability to move high-end property with speed and certainty. - The sale also fed the company’s Key For Key® giving program, which funds new homes for families in need through Giveback Homes.
What happened: - Concierge Auctions held its annual Hong Kong Global Sale live at The Upper House in Hong Kong. - The auction featured marquee properties in New York, Texas, Florida, Colorado, Wisconsin, and the Dordogne region of France. - The event generated more than US$350 million in aggregate bids. - Thirty-nine property connoisseurs bid by telephone and online from four continents and 15 U.S. states. - The auction totaled 105 bids. - Frank Trunzo, Concierge Auctions’ Head Auctioneer, conducted the sale. - Chad Roffers, CEO and Co-Founder of Concierge Auctions, called the result a demonstration of what happens when exceptional real estate meets qualified buyers on a global stage.
The details: - Renamor at 120 Ridge Road in Tuxedo Park, Hudson Valley, New York, sold for US$10.711 million. - Renamor spans more than 150 private acres and adjoins nearly 2,000 acres of protected parkland and bridle trails, about 50 minutes from Manhattan. - The 1928 French Provincial estate includes three residences totaling more than 22,000 square feet, a boathouse, log cabin, spa, tea house, tennis court, dual pools, and a net-zero microgrid. - Domaine de Ballerand in the Dordogne region of France sold for €1.955 million. - Domaine de Ballerand is a 15th-century château on wooded grounds with six private lakes and terrain for hunting, fishing, shooting, hiking, and cycling. - The French property also includes helicopter access and outbuildings and apartments that support private retreat, event, or boutique hospitality uses. - 10663 Memorial Drive in Houston sold for US$3.326 million. - The Houston home sits in Hunters Creek Village and includes walls of glass, a climate- and humidity-controlled indoor pool, a main-level primary suite, Control4 automation, a media room, a game room, an elevator, and a four-car garage. - 4901 Cimarron Mountain Road, between Telluride and Crested Butte, Colorado, sold for US$10.147 million. - Hideaway Creek Cabin is the only completed residence in the 1,900-acre Cimarron Mountain Club. - The furnished 2025 cabin sits on more than 35 acres and includes access to private snowcat skiing across more than twice the skiable terrain of Aspen Mountain. - 6941 Gaston Avenue in Dallas sold for US$2.875 million. - The Lakewood château was built in 1927 for R. L. Thornton and retains original iron gates, stone walkways, a moat, sculptures, water features, archways, and a castle turret. - The Dallas property sits on nearly one acre and includes two offices, two family rooms, two dining areas, a basement wine room, and an open bar. - 701 West Walcott Street in the Dallas area sold for US$2.367 million. - The renovated 15-plus-acre estate overlooks Lake Ray Roberts and includes a one-bedroom casita, guest house, workshop, kennels, cross-fenced pastures, a private well, a safe room, and a gated entrance. - 408 Bella Vista Way East on Sanibel Island sold for US$1.634 million. - The Gulf-front villa sits in Colony Beach Estates near the Sanibel Lighthouse and includes Gulf views from both living levels, a private elevator, a heated pool and spa, impact-rated windows and doors, and a standing-seam metal roof. - 55 Utopia Circle in Door County sold for US$3.664 million. - The Sturgeon Bay estate was rebuilt in 2024 across three waterfront parcels and includes nearly 600 feet of frontage reaching both Lake Michigan and the bay, plus a 100-foot deep-water permanent pier. - The Wisconsin property also includes natural stone, smart-home systems, an elevator, a re-engineered shoreline, and a covered outdoor kitchen.
Between the lines: - The results suggest luxury buyers are still willing to compete hard for rare, well-located properties with distinctive features and strong narratives. - The broad geographic spread of bidders points to continued international interest in auction-driven luxury real estate. - Concierge Auctions is leaning into live events as a way to create urgency ahead of its London Global Sale and End of Year Sale.
What's next: - Concierge Auctions is now accepting consignments for its London Global Sale and End of Year Sale. - The company says upcoming live sales in London, New York, and other locations will continue through the end of the year. - Property details, diligence documents, images, and showings are available through more information. - Concierge Auctions says private showings are available by appointment, in person or virtually. - The company says it continues to accept inquiries by phone at +1.212.202.2940.
The bottom line: - Concierge Auctions turned its Hong Kong sale into a global bidding event that cleared a high bar for demand, reach, and premium-property competition.
