Aviator Casino game is a crash game popular among online casino enthusiasts. It was founded by Spribe in 2019 and has since attracted a massive following worldwide. The interface is simple to understand, and the objective is to withdraw money before the plane flies away.
Crash gambling is a rapidly growing trend in gambling. The idea behind the concept is to bet on a multiplier that increases with time. The multiplier is represented by a plane or other objects in the game. The longer the player waits before cashing out, the higher the multiplier becomes. However, the risk of crashing increases with the multiplier, so players must withdraw before the plane crashes.
The essence of the Aviator slot lies in its simplicity. The higher the plane reaches, the higher the multiplier to your winning wager. The player thus must decide when to cash out before the plane crashes, and the multiplier resets to zero.
Moreover, the Aviator online game’s popularity in South Africa can be attributed to its simple playability, high payouts, and excitement that comes with it. The game also has a massive following in the country, since it’s easy to play Aviator game from mobile devices.
How to play Aviator: Game pattern
To play, place your Aviator bet on the two available options at the bottom of the screen. You can place different or the same amount bets on the same round. Then, you need to click the cash-out button before the plane crashes to win; otherwise, you will lose.
Slot interface is designed to be user-friendly and intuitive.
At the top right-hand side of the interface is a menu button that, when clicked, reveals several options, including sound, music, animation, free bets, provably fair settings, rules, and betting history.
Adjacent to the menu button is where the account balance is displayed. An animated plane is also located below the round history that illustrates how the plane flies as the multiplier increases.
Additionally, players can place their bets in two sections. These two sections can be minimized to one by clicking the (-) button on the far right of the bet button, vertically below the menu button.
Next to the bet/cash out button is the (-) and (+) signs that allow players to decrease or increase their wager amounts.
The autoplay and auto cash-out buttons are located below the bet/cash-out button and are used to set Aviator betting limits and desired multipliers.
