I have noticed a problem with Avast!, and I think the problem started with version 6.0.1203, but I’m not entierly sure.
The problem occurs when I open Avast! (double clicking on the sys tray icon) and choose to manually update the program. If there’s an update, even if it’s only a VPS update, all gadgets in Windows is closed (or possible crashes).
I’m not using the Avast! gadget, and I’ve uninstalled it from Add/Remove programs (back when it was first introduced). I’m running an English Windows 7 SP1 x64 and a Professional license of Avast!.
I would also appreciate if the Release history on Avast.com was updated more promptly. If I remember correct, it took almost a week after the release of 6.0.1125 until the Release history was updated. And the newest version has still not been added.
It don’t think that I’m the only one who wants to see what’s been changed before updating an application.

