From the Bench: Hymnody, Tunes, & Text
Notes About Sunday’s Music
June 17th, 2018 - The 11th Sunday in Ordinary Time
HYMNODY, TUNES, & TEXTS
You might have noticed that from time to time the music that we sing at Mass does not line up with the notes on the page, but somehow, the words still work. The concept of singing a text to different tunes is not new, in fact, this practice can be traced back hundreds of years to medieval times in Europe. Hymnodists would often write new words to familiar tunes, and vice versa. Because the reproduction of musical scores was expensive, it was common for hymn texts to be printed by themselves. Texts with the same meter (the number of syllables in each line of a stanza) could be sung interchangeably with melodies of the same meter. I’ll give you an example: both “Alleluia Sing to Jesus” (953) and “Joyful, Joyful, We Adore You” (611) have the same meter. If you look at the bottom of the page, the hymn tune aka melody is listed in all capital letters, in the case HYFRYDOL and ODE TO JOY. This is followed by the meter, which in this case is 8 7 8 7 D. There are several other Hymns that share this meter but are set to a different melody such as number 854 “God of Day and God of Darkness” to BEACH SPRING, or number 599 “God We Praise You” to NETTLETON. You can sing the words of any of these songs to the tunes of the others. Give it a try! We use this concept regularly here at St. Ben’s to sing a variety of beautiful texts to familiar hymn tunes. For the next several weeks we will be adding a new tune to our repertoire called RUSTINGTON. Today’s entrance is set to this tune, and it is one of my favorites. It might not be familiar at first, but we will be learning it together over the next several months.
A SPECIAL THANK YOU
Summer is when our choirs take a much needed break. I just wanted to extend a word of thanks to our outstanding choirs for all of their hard work this year. You have helped our congregation to pray well and have truly enhanced our liturgies. Thank you! I will also be taking a vacation for the next two weeks and traveling to Taiwan, Malaysia, and Singapore. Please pray for me as I embark on this adventure! I will not be writing for the next couple weeks as I travel. Please check back again in July for more "from the bench"!
592 God Has Spoken Through His Prophets
Mass of the Spirit Wind
Land of Rest Mass
938 Bread of Life from Heaven
578 How Great Thou Art
Want to know what we're singing next week? Click here for the latest congregational music schedule.

Every comparison of Linear and Jira ends the same way. Linear is the racecar. Jira is the fortress. Cool. I do not run an engineering department. I run client work. The card has a person, a due date, a conversation, and later an hour someone has to invoice. Linear does not care about that hour. Jira will let you plugin your way there until the board needs a part-time admin.
| Tides compared with Linear, Jira, Trello |  |  |  |  | 
| Topic | Tides | Linear | Jira | Trello | 
| Simple? | Name the columns. Drag a card. Done. | Even simpler, if you accept their defaults | No. That is the product. | The simplest. On purpose. | 
| Detailed? | Client, time, docs, agent inbox | Issue, cycle, Git. Not a client. | As detailed as you can stand | A card and some stickers | 
| Time | On the task. TurtleTime if you bill. | Not the job | A plugin, usually | Power-Up | 
| Who it is for | Studios shipping client work | Software teams | Orgs with process | Anyone with a wall | 
| Agent intake | agent-inbox column. Human throws it back. | An issue, if you paste it | A scheme, if you build it | A list you name Inbox | 
| Time ledger | Same core.TimeEntry as TurtleTime | Not the job | Tempo or a plugin | A Power-Up | 
| Automations | Composio: GitHub assigned → Tides task | Native Git, not your calendar | Automation + marketplace | Butler | 
| Documents | Search Kraken from the task | A link, if you remember | Confluence macro | An attachment | 
- Pick Tides if The board is how you deliver for a client, and the hour on the card has to mean the same thing as the timer.
- Pick Linear if You are a product-engineering team. You live in GitHub. You want keyboard speed and you will not invoice from the issue.
- Pick Jira if You need schemes, JQL, audit trails, or a customer who already speaks Atlassian. Do not fight that.
- Pick Trello if You want a wall of cards this afternoon and you do not need time, clients or an agent column.
Asana is in this conversation too. It is the cross-functional planner. Fine for marketing and ops portfolios. It still does not know the hour you just tracked. I left it out of the table because the real fork is simple versus detailed, and Asana sits in a third building.
What we kept simple
Statuses you can name. A board, a list, an overview. Assign, comment, attach, move on. No workflow engine. No certification. If your team needs a meeting to add a column, the tool already lost.
What we kept detailed
The project belongs to a workspace and usually a client. Time can live on the card. A Kraken page can hang off it. Shelly does not spray tasks into the void — it lands in a column called agent-inbox, and a human can throw it back. That is the detail Linear treats as someone else’s problem, and the detail Jira buries under schemes.
What is actually wired
- Statuses you name, including a seeded agent-inbox slug. Shelly’s intake is that column, not a second product.
- Task time entries write the shared core.TimeEntry ledger. TurtleTime reports them. The JWT is still a Tides JWT.
- A “Track with TurtleTime” deep link carries the task. You do not retype the project name.
- Composio rules (admin/owner): github.issue_assigned can mint a Tides task. Incoming events are idempotent by workspace, provider and external key.
- Projects and tasks can link Kraken documents. Search results still pass Kraken’s visibility, not Tides’.
- Mattermost notifications use a scoped API key. The plugin does not borrow your browser token.
- Board, list and timeline on the same project. BlockNote on the card. Tags, templates, relations, attachments on private Tides R2.
I would rather be a slightly boring board that invoices than a beautiful issue tracker that cannot.
If you are twenty engineers and the work is the repo, use Linear. Seriously. If a regulator wants Jira, use Jira. Tides is for the rest of us: the studio that has a board, a clock, and a client who does not care which framework you like.
Use Tides when you want Linear’s calm without pretending you are a GitHub-only team, and Jira’s substance without hiring a Jira person.

Over the past decade, vaping has surged in popularity, with millions of people turning to e-cigarettes as an alternative to smoking. Initially marketed as a safer option, vaping has now been linked to its own set of health risks, including lung conditions, nicotine addiction, and increased anxiety levels. While some individuals use vaping to quit traditional smoking, many find themselves trapped in a new cycle of dependency. Breaking free from this habit can be challenging, but hypnotherapy offers a powerful and lasting solution.
Many individuals who attempt to quit vaping struggle with withdrawal symptoms, cravings, and stress. The habit becomes ingrained in daily routines, making it difficult to break the cycle. Traditional methods such as nicotine patches, gum, or medications often fail to address the psychological dependency associated with vaping. Hypnotherapy, however, works on a deeper subconscious level, helping individuals rewire their thought patterns and develop a healthier mindset towards quitting.
Hypnotherapy is an effective and scientifically-backed approach to overcoming addictive behaviors. By accessing the unconscious mind, hypnotherapy can help reprogram thought processes that reinforce the vaping habit.
Through powerfful hypnotic techniques,
individuals can break free from the mental and emotional grip of vaping, making the transition to a vape-free life much easier.
One of the key aspects of successfully quitting vaping is managing stress. Many people turn to vaping as a coping mechanism for stress, anxiety, or boredom.
Hypnotherapy not only helps remove the urge to vape but also teaches powerful relaxation techniques.
By addressing the root causes of stress and providing healthier coping strategies, hypnotherapy significantly increases the chances of long-term success.
Why I Am the Ideal Choice to Help You Quit Vaping
With 22 years of experience as a highly respected and recommended London hypnotherapist, I have helped countless individuals overcome their vaping addiction. My approach is personalized, compassionate, and results-driven, ensuring that each client receives the support they need to achieve lasting change. My expertise in hypnotherapy makes me the ideal choice for anyone looking to quit vaping for good.
Personalized Sessions Tailored to Your Needs
Every individual’s vaping habit is unique, which is why I tailor each hypnotherapy session to the specific needs of my clients. By understanding your triggers, behaviors, and motivations, I create a customized plan that maximizes your success in quitting vaping.
In-Person Hypnotherapy in London
For those who prefer face-to-face sessions, I offer in-person hypnotherapy appointments in London. Meeting in a calming and professional environment allows clients to fully immerse themselves in the therapeutic process and gain the most from each session.
Convenient Home Visits for Comfort and Ease
I also provide home visit sessions for clients who prefer to quit vaping in the comfort of their own space. This personalized approach ensures that clients feel relaxed and supported throughout their journey to a vape-free life.
Online Hypnotherapy: Helping Clients Worldwide
For those who are unable to meet in person, my highly popular online hypnotherapy sessions offer the same effectiveness as in-person meetings. With clients from all over the world, I have successfully helped individuals quit vaping through virtual sessions, providing the flexibility and accessibility needed for lasting results.
How Online Hypnotherapy Works
Using secure and easy-to-use video conferencing platforms, my online hypnotherapy sessions allow clients to receive expert guidance from anywhere in the world. Whether you are at home or traveling, my online sessions provide the same high-quality experience, ensuring you stay on track with your goals.
Overcoming Vaping Cravings with Hypnotherapy
Cravings are one of the biggest obstacles to quitting vaping. Hypnotherapy helps reprogram the subconscious mind to remove the desire for vaping and replace it with positive, healthier alternatives. By addressing the psychological dependency, clients find it easier to resist cravings and stay committed to quitting.
Strengthening Willpower and Motivation
Many individuals struggle with willpower when attempting to quit vaping. Hypnotherapy boosts motivation by reinforcing positive behaviors and attitudes towards quitting. By strengthening your determination, you will find it much easier to stay vape-free for the long term.
Achieving Long-Term Success
Quitting vaping is not just about stopping a habit; it’s about creating a healthier, more fulfilling lifestyle. My hypnotherapy sessions provide clients with the tools and mindset necessary for long-term success. By building new habits and reinforcing a positive self-image, clients experience lasting transformation.
Client Success Stories
Over the years, I have worked with countless individuals who have successfully quit vaping through hypnotherapy. Their stories serve as a testament to the power of this method in helping people reclaim control over their health and well-being.
Take the First Step Towards a Vape-Free Life With Hypnotherapy
If you are ready to quit vaping for good, hypnotherapy is the most effective and lasting solution. Whether you choose in-person sessions in London, home visits, or online hypnotherapy, I am here to guide and support you every step of the way. Contact me today to begin your journey to a healthier, vape-free life.
