- TRINITY YACHTS
Built in aluminum by Trinity Yachts, Themis was delivered in October 1998 and is a 1999 model, and has been maintained to ABS and AMS class. A high-volume interior has been decorated by Dee Robinson and features mahogany and African pear wood joinery. Themis underwent a full refit in 2015 meaning she has been brought up to modern standards and is in pristine condition.
The salon, formal dining and skylounge area are spacious and comfortable making for wonderful relaxation and dining areas. Extensive deck areas have plenty of room for outdoor activities including a large flybridge with a bar, settee, sunlounges and a six-person jacuzzi. Powered by twin Caterpillar 2250 HP main engines with low original hours and equipped with twin Caterpillar 99KW generators. Other features include full walk around decks, Naiad stabilizers, bow thruster, Atlas shore power converter and 22' Nautica tender.
Themis accommodates 10 guests in five staterooms. These include an on-deck master suite with a king sized bed, two VIP staterooms with king size beds, Queen and twin staterooms below. All staterooms have private baths, showers and jacuzzi tubs.
The particulars on this page are a general guide to give a broad description of the yacht. They are not intended to constitute part of an offer or contract. All prices, photographs, measurements, plans and specifications referred to are given as a guide only and should not be relied upon for the charter of this yacht. The copyright of all details,photographs and deckplans remains the property of their respectful owners.

Debuting at the iconic IRONMAN World Championship in Kona, Hawaii, you may have spotted a new performance cooling garment with a twist. While all eyes are on the competitors, behind the scenes, support crews work tirelessly to ensure the athletes are race-ready. Among them, bike mechanics labor in the sweltering heat, making sure the bikes for 2,400 competitors are in peak condition. For these hard-working mechanics, we’ve developed the Glacier Apron—a cooling solution designed to keep them comfortable as they work.
A work apron for bike mechanics must be a functional extension of their clothing, with pockets for tools and bike parts within easy reach. However, traditional aprons can become hot and uncomfortable, especially when temperatures soar, leaving mechanics drenched in sweat.
As the world’s best bike mechanics gather in Kona, we created custom Glacier Aprons specifically designed for Ceramic Speed mechanics to enhance cooling and keep them cooler while they work. The Glacier Apron is versatile for year-round use, but for hotter conditions, it can be briefly soaked in water to activate an endothermic reaction, drawing heat away from the body and providing a cooling effect. Importantly, the apron is designed to keep the mechanic dry while delivering this cooling benefit.
The result? The Ceramic Speed mechanics can expect to stay cooler, sweat less, and feel more comfortable while working at events or outdoors in warm and hot conditions.
The Glacier Apron is crafted from premium-quality materials and our advanced cooling textiles, ensuring both durability and comfort. Features such as wide-format straps distribute weight evenly, while a magnetic fastening system makes it easy and convenient to wear.
What do you think of the Glacier Apron we created for Ceramic Speed at Kona? Would a premium quality work-apron that keeps you cool as you work be a garment you would wear? Subscribe to our newsletter (below) and follow us on social media to stay up-to-date.
If you’re interested in owning your own Glacier Apron, get in touch and let us know! If we receive strong interest, we’re eager to explore making the Glacier Apron available to all.

