As summer arrives here in Kolkata, we must prepare and protect our eyes. But people generally only take care of their skin. They must also take care of their eyes.
Eye care in summer is of utmost importance. Why? Because In summer, day time is longer than night time. Your eyes are exposed to sunlight for longer periods. Also, there is an increase in temperature. All these reasons can add up and cause eye infection in summer. If you look at the sun – the blinding light can cause eye irritation. You need the right kind of eye drops for irritated eyes, aka eye relaxation drops.
However, in spite of the reality, many of us are oblivious to sun safety. According to a report, WHO has stated that 20% of cataracts are caused by UV radiation from the sun.
According to ophthalmologist Michael Kutryb, MD, a spokesperson for the American Academy of Ophthalmology, “UV radiation from the sun can damage the eye's surface tissues as well as the cornea and the lens (Source: https://www.aao.org/eye-health/tips-prevention/sun).
Let's explore the common eye problems prevalent in summer and their remedies.
Dryness of the Eyes
According to a report, eyes become dry when the water (read tears) are not produced in sufficient quantity and thus they cannot lubricate the eyes. This may cause inflammation and may even damage the eye’s surface.
Dry eyes can cause irritation, those suffering from dry eyes must take eye care in summer as the problem may magnify due to exposure to the sunlight. If they don’t, they may feel irritation in the eyes.
Allergies of the Eyes
Allergies are usually caused by dust and pollution, which increases during summer. In a metro city like Kolkata, the pollution quotient is quite high. Allergies might turn your eyes red. They may cause itching, tearing, blurred vision, burning sensation and sensitivity to light.
However, in such conditions, eye relaxation drops from Itone may help.
The condition is also known as photokeratitis. The condition is very painful and it is caused by the UV rays of the sun. It is similar to sunburned skin, only here, the eyes are sunburned. Usually, it affects both the eyes. 
If you expose your eyes too much to the sun, this condition may develop. It may subside in a few days or the irritation may continue. If it does, eye drops for irritated eyes from Itone may help.
Conjunctivitis of the eyes  
Most people are aware of this condition. It’s a kind of eye infection. Conjunctivitis causes redness, discharge and irritation. It spreads usually during summer. Public places and offices are spots where you may be infected by this disease. 
Eye Care in Summer – Eye Drops for Irritated Eyes
We must limit direct sunlight exposure as much as possible. Itone eye drops for irritated eyes provide natural protective compounds of Neem and Tulsi. These sun-stressed eye-calming ingredients effectively manage discomfort in addition to providing relaxation to burned eyes. 
Eye drops with high lubricating properties reduce eye discomfort that develops because of wind and heat-related dryness, so common in summer.
Keep Eyes Hydrated – Eye Relaxation Drops
If you suffer from dryness of eyes or the likes, lubricant eye drops from Itone may help. Itone therapy includes Yashtimadhu and Punarnava components which balances water retention and also increases moisture in the eyes. 
The herbs present within these drops boost tear stability thus moisturizing the tear layers. This strengthens the natural tear defense system of the eyes. This eye therapy is a very effective summertime care solution.
Cleanliness of the Eyes
The Kolkata air is full of sweat and airborne contaminants. Also, dust increases in summer and it affects the eye skin and results in uncomfortable sensations from itchiness to scratchiness. It would be good to have a regular face wash. But that may not always suffice and deep cleaning may be required.
Itone Eye Drop contains antibacterial properties. Derived from Camphor and Daruharidra ingredients, they provide anti-inflammatory action on the eyes. The Ayurvedic properties in this medication makes them perfect for the eyes. There will not be any burning sensations. Also, for eye lubricating use, they come handy. Regular application wipes away irritating substances and provides your eyes with freshness along with protection.
Eye Care In Summer
Your eyes are probably your biggest assets. Take proper eye care in summer. Remember, while working in the office, too much screen time also affects the eyes. You should take regular breaks in between work. 
If that is not possible use Itone eye relaxation drops. They will not only keep your eyes clean but also protect them in summer.

