Support groups are a community of people with a similar diagnosis or challenge who gather to share knowledge and encouragement.
Support groups come in many shapes and sizes. Some are large online communities with many people to answer your questions. Some are facilitated by a mental health professional, a person diagnosed with an illness, the family of someone diagnosed, or a medical expert. They can be held in person, online, or by phone. You may want to check out a few groups and formats to find one that you are comfortable in.
PCF has several private, moderated support groups on Facebook for different interests.

Passamonte is quickly making a name for herself as a pianist to watch on the international classical music scene. With here majestic interpretation of Beethoven, and now Chopin, here audiences are left wanting more and wondering where will this talented performer take them next as her bright musical future continues to unfold on recordings and in concert halls worldwide.
“Stefania Passamonte performs…at such a high level of technical expertise, musicianship, and emotion that {her albums] deserve to stand next to some of the most storied recordings made of these historic works.”
A successful recording artist and member of the Recording Academy in the USA, Stefania is an Italian concert pianist now based in London, regularly performing at major venues and with orchestras worldwide. Her playing has been praised for its “powerfully emotive lines and an impresario air…a living, breathing performance that is nothing less than stunning.”
A performance graduate from Royal Academy of Music in London and Ecole Normale in Paris, Stefania has given solo recitals in the major international concert halls, many of which were televised broadcasts, including “St Martin in The Fields” in London, National Philharmonic of Ukraine in Kiev, “Sala Puccini” in Milan, Palau da Musica in Valencia, Sibelius Hall in Finland, Varna Opera Theatre in Bulgaria, Casa da Musica in Porto.
Solo Concertos include the Lathi Symphony Orchestra under the baton of Ville Matjaeff, and the Varna Philharmonic Orchestra with conductor Stefano Seghedoni.
“She has a virtuoso flair and a great imagination but most relevant of all is perhaps that she possesses a rare gift of communication”.
Selected to perform on the stage of the most famous International Piano Competitions as the Chopin Competition of Warsaw, the “Vladimir Horowitz” of Kiev, the “Maria Canals” of Barcelona and the “Jose’ Iturbi” in Spain, the Porto Competition in Portugal and Beethoven Klavierwettewerbe of Vienna, Stefania won several awards and acknowledgements, among which the prestigious “Premio Ghirlandina” given by her native city Modena to an artist “distinguished in the international panorama for special merits and success” (fellow citizens award winners include Luciano Pavarotti and Mirella Freni).
“Italian born pianist Stefania Passamonte returns with another world-class album full of emotional and technically brilliant interpretations of some of the most beautiful and engaging works by Romantic composer Frédéric Chopin.”
She is an exclusive recording artist for Master Chord Records and her recordings with major works by Beethoven, Chopin, Schumann and the complete “Transcendental Studies” by Liszt won great acclaim from press and audiences alike. Gold Medal at The Akademia Awards in Los Angeles and Silver Medal at the Global Music Awards 2017, her new releases have been selected several times at the prestigious Grammy’s Awards in Los Angeles as best soloist and best album of the Classic fields, while she appeared to the red carpet of the Classic BRIT Awards in London in several editions. Her albums are broadcasted by the major Classical radios worldwide, including BBC Radio 3 and Classic FM in UK, while many solo recitals and concertos with the orchestra have been televised broadcasts, including RAI 3 and Sky TV in Italy, TVG in Spain, 1plus1 TV in Ukraine among the others.
“Passamonte is quickly making a name for herself as a pianist to watch on the international classical music scene. With her majestic interpretation of Beethoven, and now Chopin, her audiences are left wanting more and wondering where will this talented performer take them next as her bright musical future continues to unfold on recordings and in concert halls worldwide.”
“Passamonte si sta facendo rapidamente un nome come pianista da tenere d’occhio sulla scena nternazionale della Musica Classica. Con le sue maestose interpretazioni Beethoven e adesso Chopin, lascia il pubblico con la voglia di sapere dove li portera’ ancora questoa talentuosa concertista, visto che il suo brillante futuro musicale continua a spiegarsi in registrazioni e concerti di livello mondiale”.
“Stefania Passamonte suona…a un tale livello di virtuosismo, musicalita’ e inspirazione che [i suoi Cds] meritano di stare accanto alle registrazioni piu’ storiche di queste opere”. Artista di successo e membro della Recording Academy per i famosi Grammys Awards di Los Angeles, Stefania e’ una concertista italiana di fama internazionale che vive a Londra.
“Una musicista dal talento eccezionale”, Stefania ha tenuto concerti in tutta Europa, alcuni dei quali in diretta televisiva e radiofonica, tra cui “St Martin in The Fields” a Londra, il Teatro Filarmonico Nazionale di Kiev in Ukraina, “Sala Puccini” a Milano, il Palau da Musica di Valencia, la Sibelius Hall in Finlandia, il Teatro dell’Opera di Varna n Bulgaria, la Casa da Musica a Porto in Portogallo. Concerti solistici con l’orchestra includono la Lathi Symphony Orchestra con il direttore d’orchestra Ville Matjaeff, e la Varna Philharmonic Orchestra con il direttore d’orchestra Stefano Seghedoni.
“Possiede una grande immaginazione e tecnica virtuosistica, ma forse il suo dono piu’ raro e’ la capacita’ di comunicare col pubblico.”
Selezionata per suonare sul palcoscenico dei più grandi concorsi pianistici internazionali come il Concorso “Chopin” di Varsavia in Polonia, il “Vladimir Horowitz” di Kiev, il “Jose Iturbi” e il “Maria Canals” di Barcellona in Spagna, il Concorso di Porto in Portogallo, il Concorso “Beethoven” di Vienna o il Concorso Busoni di Bolzano, Stefania ha ottenuto numerosi premi e riconoscimenti, tra i quali il prestigioso Premio Ghirlandina, assegnatole dal Rotary Club di Modena come “Artista particolarmente distintasi nel panorama internazionale per successo e riconoscimenti”.
“Frasi di grande potenza espressiva e un’aria da maestro”
“…un’interpretazione piena di vita e respiro che non e’ niente di meno che stupefacente.”
Le sue registrazioni comprendono opere di Mozart, Beethoven, Chopin, Schumann e i “12 Studi Trascendentali di Liszt”, pubblicati dall’etichetta inglese Master Chord Records con gran successo di pubblico e critica. Medaglia d’Oro ai The Akademia Awards in Los Angeles e Medaglia d’Argento ai Global Music Awards 2017, i sui dischi concorrono annualmente ai Grammy Awards come miglior solista e miglior album della Classica, mentre e’ stata invitata sul tappeto rosso dei Classic BRITS Awards alla Royal Albert Hall di Londra in numerose edizioni. I suoi album sono trasmessi dalle maggiori radio classiche in tutto il mondo, tra cui il BBC Radio 3 e Classic FM in Gran Bretagna, mentre molti solo recital e concerti con l’orchestra sono stati trasmessi da maggiori canali televisivi, tra cui RAI 3 e Sky TV in Italia, TVG in Spagna e 1plus1 TV in Ucraina.
“La pianista italiana Stefania Passamonte ritorna con un altro album di classe mondiale, pieno di interpretazioni emozionanti e tecnicamente brillanti di alcune delle opere piu’ meravigliose e coinvolgenti del compositore Romantico Frédćric Chopin.”
“Stefania Passamonte joue…à un tel haut niveau d’expertise technique, de talent musical, et d’émotion que ses albums méritent pour se tenir après certains des enregistrements les plus légendaires fait de ces travaux historiques.”
Membre de suffrage pour les Grammy’s Awards de la Recording Academy dans les Etats-Unis D’Amérique, Stefania est une pianiste italienne vivant à Londres et avec une solide expérience qui s’élargit du récitals international à l’enregistrement soliste.
“Une jeune musicienne formidablement doué..”, Stefania a donné de nombreux récitals en tant que concertiste en toute l’Europe, certains d’entre eux ayant été retransmis à la télévision. Parmi ses engagements les plus importants notant les récitals à Saint Martin in The Fields à Londres, au Théâtre National Philharmonic de Ukraine à Kiev, la Salle Puccini à Milan, la Steinway Hall de Londres, la Sibelius Hall in Finlande, le Théâtre de l’Opera de Varna in Bulgarie et la Casa da Musica de Porto. Concerts en solo avec l’orchestre incluent l’Orchestre Symphonique de Lahti avec le chef Ville Matjaeff , et l’Orchestre Philharmonique de Varna avec le chef Stefano Seghedoni.
“Elle a un air de virtuose et une grande imagination, mais surtout elle possède un rare cadeau de communication”. Sélectionnée pour jouer sur le scènes des concours de piano internationaux les plus connu, notamment le “Concours Chopin” de Varsovie, le Concours “Vladimir Horowitz” de Kiev, le Concours “Maria Canals” de Barcelona et “Jose Iturbi” de Valencia en Espagne, le Concours Citade Do Porto en Portugal, le Concours Beethoven de Vienna et le Concours Busoni de Bolzano, Stefania a été lauréate de nombreux bourses et a obtenu la prestigieuse distinction de “Premio Ghirlandina” décernée par le Rotary Club de Modène, récompensant un artiste de Modène pour l’ensemble de ses activités artistiques internationales.
“ Lignes puissamment émotives et un air d’impresario…”
“…une exécution vif et respirant qui rien n’est moins que stupéfiant”
Ses enregistrements incluent les majeures compositions par Bach, Mozart, Beethoven, Chopin, Schumann. les complètes “Etudes d’exécution transcendante” de Liszt relâché par Master Chord Records avec grand succès de critiques et de public. Medaille d’Or au The Akademia Awards a Los Angeles et Medaille d’Argente au Global Music Awards 2017, ses nouveaux albums sont régulièrement sélectionné pour les catégories de “Meilleure Album” et “Meilleure Soliste” de la Musique Classique aux Grammy’s Awards de Los Angeles (USA), aussi bien que depuis le 2012 elle est présente chaque année sur le Tapis Rouge du Classic BRITS Awards de Londres (UK)
Ses albums sont diffusés par les principales radios classiques du monde, y compris BBC Radio 3 et Classic FM au Royaume-Uni, tandis que de nombreux récitals et concertos solo avec l’orchestre ont été télévisées, y compris RAI 3 et Sky TV en Italie, TVG en Espagne, 1plus1 TV En Ukraine parmi les autres.
“La pianiste Italienne Stefania Passamonte retourne avec un autre album de renommée internationale plein d’interprétations émotives et techniquement brillantes de certains des plus beaux et charmants ouvres par le compositeur Romantique Frédćric Chopin.”
“Passamonte est en train de se faire reconnaître rapidement comme un pianiste a regarder sur la scène de la musique classique internationale.
Avec ses interprétations majestueuses de Beethoven, et maintenant Chopin, ses audiences sont parties vouloir plus et se demandent où cette interprète doué les prendra après, puisque son brillant avenir musical continue à se déplier sur les enregistrements et dans les salles de concert mondiales ».

Alleging large-scale irregularities in the Navi Mumbai Municipal Corporation’s (NMMC) nala-cleaning work, Sajag Nagrik Manch has claimed that the drive has turned into a “treasury-cleaning operation” rather than drain-cleaning.
Information obtained under the RTI Act 2005 has revealed that a whopping Rs 59.54 lakh was shown as expenditure for desilting five drains in the Belapur division. According to records, 6,043 cubic metres (around 7,500–8,000 tonnes) of silt were allegedly removed, requiring about 1,223 truck trips. The work order, however, was issued only in August, months after the tender process began in May.
Ground Reality Mismatches Claims
Members of Sajag Nagrik Manch conducted spot inspections and found that the actual desilting work was nowhere close to what was shown in official records. " For instance, while the administration claimed 180 truckloads of silt were removed from a drain in Sector 30/31, residents reported that only a handful of labourers worked with shovels and baskets for a few days, mainly clearing weeds," said a member.
Locals also noted that such huge quantities of silt never existed in the drains. Similar discrepancies were found at other sites.
The Manch has demanded an independent inquiry into all nala-cleaning works in Navi Mumbai, public disclosure of truck numbers, dumping locations, transport permits and CCTV footage, and criminal cases against contractors and officials involved. They also sought adoption of AI-based monitoring, timely tendering of future works, publication of a white paper on the last three years’ nala-cleaning expenses, and uploading of all related details on NMMC’s website.
Warning of “Mithi River-Style Corruption”
“This is not drain-cleaning but direct treasury-cleaning. The situation is a repeat of the Mithi River corruption scandal in Mumbai,” the Manch warned.
Copies of the complaint have been submitted to the Municipal Commissioner, Lokayukta, Chief Minister’s Secretariat, Anti-Corruption Bureau, Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG), and the Urban Development Department.
Local resident and Manch member Bhimrao Jamkhandikar said: “On May 26, after heavy rains, water flowed smoothly through the Sector 30/31 drain. There was hardly any silt. At most, one or two truckloads could have been removed. Every building here has CCTV cameras, and footage can verify the actual desilting.”

