Start strong with a 1.2-mile (1.9K) swim in the calm Pacific. We focus your early weeks on technique with guided swim drills and video instruction. You'll develop open water skills, pacing, and efficiency—all essential for the mild 66–70°F (19–21°C) water temps you'll face on race day.
🚴 Bike the Costa Verde with Power and Precision
Peru’s 56-mile (90K) closed-course bike leg is flat and fast. Our plan ramps you up with structured heart rate and RPE-based sessions, building the stamina to hold consistent speed across three loops. Progressive brick workouts prepare you to transition seamlessly into the run—just like on race day.
🏃 Run Strong Along Lima’s Beachfront
The 13.1-mile (21.1K) run course is flat but exposed. With three loops and coastal views, mental focus and pace control are key. We incorporate tempo runs, endurance builds, and strength work to sharpen your run form and mental toughness—perfect for those final miles to the finish at Agua Dulce Beach.
