New Delhi. : The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) has officially released the notification for 25,487 General Duty (GD) Constable posts for the 2026 recruitment cycle. The vacancies span across various Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs), the Secretariat Security Force (SSF), and the Rifleman (GD) cadre in Assam Rifles.
The positions fall under the Level-3 pay matrix, offering a salary range of ₹21,700 to ₹69,100. Eligible candidates who have passed Class 10 can now apply through the official SSC portal, ssc.gov.in. The Computer-Based Test (CBT) is tentatively scheduled to be conducted between February and April 2026.
Total Vacancies Across Forces
Out of the total 25,487 posts,
- 23,467 vacancies are earmarked for male candidates
- 2,020 vacancies are designated for female candidates
The category-wise distribution is as follows:
- SC: 3,702
- ST: 2,313
- OBC: 5,765
- EWS: 2,605
- UR: 11,102
Selected candidates will serve in forces such as BSF, CISF, CRPF, SSB, ITBP, Assam Rifles, and SSF, depending on vacancy allocation and merit ranking.
- Last date to apply: December 31, 2025 (11 PM)
- Last date for fee payment: January 1, 2026
- Correction window: January 8 to January 10, 2026
During the correction period, candidates may edit details in their forms and pay applicable correction fees, if required.
- To be eligible for SSC GD Constable posts:
- Candidates must be 18 to 23 years old.
- SC/ST applicants get 5-year age relaxation.
- OBC candidates and ex-servicemen get 3-year relaxation.
- Applicants must have passed Class 10 from a recognised board.
- NCC certificate holders will receive an additional 5% incentive during the recruitment process.
As per SSC guidelines, ex-servicemen include individuals who have served in the Regular Army, Navy, or Air Force in any rank, whether combatant or non-combatant.
How to Apply
Candidates applying for the first time must complete the One-Time Registration (OTR) on the SSC website.
After logging in with OTR credentials:
- Open the SSC GD Constable 2026 application link
- Fill in personal, academic, and communication details
- Upload required documents
- Pay the ₹100 application fee
- Submit the online form
Once submitted successfully, the candidate’s application will be considered for the 2026 SSC GD recruitment cycle.
