Oleksandr's instructions do not work if the account is no longer valid but still registered in the Microsoft Authenticator app. It requires the user to sign into the old invalid account which makes no sense because the account is no longer valid and you're stuck with the account unable to remove it. Microsoft dropped the ball with that one and they need to fix it.
My account got added to someone else's personal authenticator. He can't sign into the account on the authenticator app as it asks for a code from the authenticator app itself. So, the steps listed are unhelpful. I also cannot log into the security settings as it asks for a code match or a 6-digit code again from the authenticator app. So how can I fix this? The person in question doesn't need to know anything on my account much less have access to changes on it.
I'm still having the issue after following the steps above,
