It is not listed under Settings / Accounts
I can login into the work account, then it is no longer greyed out, I can select the three dots and remove, but this only brings it back to greyed out
I have tried the clear cache approach, did not work
I manage student accounts. For one student account, I tried more than ten times and was always prompted with ‘Account removed from app,’ but it still appears on the list.
I tried unregistering my old company from the device and it prompted me to enter in a new company. But it did not let me delete or remove the old one as a default.
It seems Microsoft no longer supports this product. I could try uninstalling and reinstalling the app, but there's a risk I won't be able to access the current system if I run into a problem.
I have not logged into the account as the account was already added in another mobile MS authenticator app.
All I need to remove from my mobile which is not required in my mobile? Why the removal of account should is complicated where that account logged in was not successful?
I have found a workaround to remove an old accounts from your Microsoft Authenticator app on an Android.
If you have an android mobile, follow the instructions below:
Open your mobiles' Settings, then tap on Users & accounts or Accounts and backup (depends on the android version).
Scroll down and look for Microsoft old account(s) you want to remove or Work account and tap on it.
Once you found the required account, tap on it and select More or tap on 2 dots : (depends on the android version) in the upper right corner of your screen.
Select Remove account. You may need to repeat it twice or thrice.
Once account has removed, close the Microsoft Authenticator app if already opened.
Now tap and hold on Microsoft Authenticator app, and select App info.
Select Storage usage > Under Cache, tap on Clear cache.
Open Microsoft Authenticator app, and old account(s) should not appear now.
Thank you Mr. Dhiman! This worked perfectly. Left a job with logins still on the phone/in Authenticator which no longer work, so completely understand Scott's problem below. Well written steps, Deepak! Especially the need for multiple "remove account" taps! (I did.) Have bookmarked/saved the steps for exit interviewers.
With the latest Android. Accounts and backup > manage accounts, then scroll through your list of accounts, removing only the ones you need to remove (eg. If you've left your job that might be Outlook. I had an employee ID as one account and an employee email for something else, so had to remove both.)
I manage students' accounts. one account had problem with MFA. I disabled the MFA, but still ask MFA with Authenticator. So, I tried that account on my two phones. The authenticator app always said the “QR code already used” and the account on the Authenticator shows "Sign in". I clicked the account, it asked me "To set up Microsoft Authenticator, you will need to go to aka.ms/mfasetup on a web browser". It is in the loop and unable to make MFA works for this strange account.
the account is in "Sign in" status. Didn't has 3 dots. I am managing students accounts. Only one account could not work with Athenticator , even I disable the MFA /enforce/reset password/change phones.
Worked perfectly for me, I was struggling to find a way to delete / remove the old work account from the MS Authenticator app and this was the solution, thank you!
In the new version of android it's now called "Passwords, passkeys & accounts" go down to accounts, scroll to the email you want removed, click it, hit remove account. Done!
that was also a solution that worked for me, the old account was not possible to remove in authenticator app but when i removed it in android settings it was also removed in the app. Thanks for this solution
I have the problem balintn describes. On step 3, if I tap the old account I want to remove, it automatically does some multiple redirection stuff and tells me to sign in and offers some help with signing in. But there is no option to remove the account.
In my case, there is no option for "Remove the account". It showed only : "Accont name: Live". I tried more than 50 times for this account and never got removed.
I managed sutdents' account on my phone and only had one account as I mentioned could not removed.
I'm in the same boat as John Hsu. I have no "Remove" button for the account I want to remove.
However, I was able to create a new entry for the same account since it is still active. I just now have 2 listings for the account. Aggravating, but at least I've made it work for me.
This worked for me on my Google Pixel 6 Pro:
Open "Settings", then "Passwords, passkeys & accounts", click on the account to be removed and then click on "Remove account".
When I went back into Authenticator, the account was gone!
For those still having their old accounts still listed, I found the missing step. After step 6 above, a login prompt will likely pop up for that account. Don't close the screen or use your phone's back button. Instead, click the <- to the left of your account email. Your authenticator app will refresh with that account having been removed.
It's that click of that little <- button that makes it work.
I did this. (Some time ago, there was no "Remove" button if I wasn't logged in that account, now there is. That's good.) I got a message that the account was removed, but the account entry only blinked somewhat. Like got removed and immediately reappeared back. I killed the app and re-opened it – yep, the account is still there...
