Programme modules.
The components we combine into a programme. Filter by region, season and group size, or send us the brief and we will do the combining.
Heated tipis in the dark zone, an open fire, a photographer on site. Nothing is promised, the odds are good.
Floating in a survival suit in an opened lake, under the aurora. Guided, about one hour.
Dinner on the fell
A fell-top restaurant taken privately, with the descent by snowmobile sled or gondola.
Exclusive-use fell lodge
A whole lodge of suites and glass igloos held for one group, with meetings in the restaurant and no other guests.
Glass igloo buyout
A glass-igloo village held for one group. Aurora wake-up alerts on request.
Husky & reindeer
Husky and reindeer sleigh rides with a herder briefing. Runs in parallel for larger groups.
Husky safari, half day
Longer teams and trails for guests who want to drive rather than sit. Farm visit and lunch included.
Ice fishing and lunch on the ice
Drilled holes, guides, and salmon soup cooked over a fire on the frozen lake.
A lake-ice circuit with karts on studded tyres, run as a competition for the group alone.
Lappish dinner in a log hut
Reindeer, fish and berries served around an open fire in a traditional kota.
Midnight sun hike
A guided evening walk on the fell with dinner at the top, in daylight at eleven at night.
Night in a design suite above the treeline
One night in a glass-fronted suite, dinner in the house restaurant, aurora from the bed.
Private aurora hunt
Minivans and a guide who reads the cloud forecast and drives to the gap in it.
Private dinner inside snow
Dinner in a snow venue: packed snow walls, ice glasses, hot food, thermal seating.
Private fell villa with chef
A log villa on the fell, held exclusively, with private chef, driver and guides. Sauna, outdoor jacuzzi, aurora from the terrace.
Rally driving on ice
Rally cars, buggies and cross-cars on a purpose-built ice track with instructors. Half a day.
Reindeer farm with a herder
Feeding, a short sleigh run, and the herder's account of how the year works.
Rafts and guides on a class II river, with a sauna and dinner at the landing.
Sámi culture day, Inari
The Siida museum, a reindeer herding family and lunch on the shore of Lake Inari. A full day from Saariselkä.
Smoke sauna and ice swimming
A lakeside smoke sauna, a hole cut in the ice and a guide who talks people in and out of the water.
Snow castle and ice bar
An excursion to a hotel built of snow and ice, with a guided tour and a drink in the ice bar.
Guided trail safari, one or two per machine, thermal suits issued. Two-hour loop or a full day with lunch on the ice.
Snowshoe walk with a fire stop
The gentlest arctic module, for mixed fitness levels. Hot drinks and sausages over a fire mid-way.
Sport driving on ice
Studded tyres on a lake circuit with an instructor in the car. Coffee tent between runs.
Winter clothing for the whole stay
Thermal overalls, boots, mittens and hats sized from a pre-trip form and fitted on arrival.
Dinner in the hunting lodge
Salmon cooked over an open fire, long tables, one room for the whole group.
E-mountain bikes and canoes
A lake afternoon split between guided e-bike trails and canoeing, with a floating option.
Floating in dry suits
Lying on your back in a frozen lake, fully dry, looking at the sky.
Lakeside villa resort in exclusive use
Villas, a meeting building and a spa two hours from Helsinki Airport, taken as a unit.
National park day, Nuuksio
Forty minutes from Helsinki: a guided hike, a team problem-solving exercise and lunch in a lakeside venue.
Private spa evening
Sauna, infinity pool and hot tub held for the group for two hours.
Racing snowmobiles on a field track
Test drives on racing machines with an instructor, followed by a trail loop.
Rally Finland travel and VIP package
Official VIP products with hotel, transfers and stage logistics, as one package.
Saimaa Cycle Tour team package
Entry support, hotels, bike transport and official hospitality products for teams and companies.
Banquet in Turku Castle
Dinner in the Renaissance hall of a 13th-century castle, with a guided tour of the halls beforehand.
Distillery visit and tasting
A small island distillery, a tour and a gin tasting on the way to the outer archipelago.
Island lunch in Nauvo
Ferry and coach to a harbour village, lunch at the water, time to walk.
King's Gate arrival, Suomenlinna
Private wooden boats from Market Square through the King's Gate to Suomenlinna. 20 minutes.
Lighthouse island overnight
A night on an outer-archipelago island reached by ferry or boat, dinner in the pilot village.
Lunch on an island fortress
Suomenlinna by private boat, a walk through the tunnels and lunch inside the walls.
Private archipelago cruise
A chartered ship from Market Square, a guide on board, three hours among the islands.
Private island for a board retreat
A former coast-guard station on its own Baltic island: twelve bedrooms, a boardroom in the watchtower, three saunas and a host who cooks with what the island and the sea provide.
Guided paddling between skerries, sized to the group, with a shore lunch.
Traditional sailing vessel
A day under sail among the islands on a restored wooden ship, with the crew and lunch on board.
Turku and the archipelago
A banquet in the Renaissance hall of a 13th-century castle, a day among the islands by boat, kayak or wooden sailing vessel, and a closing dinner in Turku's old railway works.
Underground smoke sauna
The largest of its kind, plus seaside saunas and a plunge into the Baltic, at a fishing village turned venue.
Aalto and Turku, three days
Turku Castle and Cathedral, Paimio Sanatorium by Aino and Alvar Aalto, with Finlandia Hall and Villa Mairea as Helsinki and Noormarkku extensions, a night in the former Kakola prison hotel and the archipelago's smoke saunas. Built for groups who know their architecture.
Airport meet and greet
Named hosts at the gate, transfers sized per flight, luggage handled separately when the programme needs it.
Architecture walk with an architect
Oodi, Amos Rex and Finlandia Hall on foot, led by a practising architect.
Awards gala production
Venue, staged LED screen, sound and light, a four-course dinner and a performance, under one production lead.
Brewery tour and dinner
A tour and tasting at a city brewery, dinner in the same building.
Concert-hall dinner, Finlandia Hall
Dinner on the stage or in the foyer of Alvar Aalto's hall, with staging and sound if the evening needs it.
Design district walk
Studios, makers and shops with a design specialist, fifteen guests per guide.
Guided shoreline and harbour route. Electric assistance keeps mixed fitness levels together.
Figure Skating Worlds 2027 hospitality
Official hospitality produced by Elämys DMC: tickets, lounge or seated dining, hotel and transfers, for companies, groups and individual visitors.
Four restaurants, four evenings
A dining sequence across the city's best tables with a host at every dinner.
Gala in the National Museum
The museum closed to the public, arrival through the stone hall, dinner under the vaults.
Host company visit
Ninety minutes with the leadership of a Finnish company in the group's own sector, arranged through our network.
Market hall tasting walk
Old Market Hall and the harbour with a food guide, tasting as you go.
Meeting room with hybrid set-up
Private floor, technician on site, redundant connection, catering held in the room.
Private concert in the Rock Church
Temppeliaukio taken for the group with a short concert on its acoustics.
Private sauna island
A whole island twenty minutes from the centre: smoke saunas, hot tubs, staff and the boat back.
Public sauna taken privately
A waterfront sauna held for the group, with a ladder into the sea and a bar.
Sea sauna evening, Helsinki
Private sauna on the sea with a ladder into the Baltic and a bar. Works as a meeting venue.
Tallinn for a day
Ferry across, four local guides in the old town, lunch, business-class ferry back.
The sequence matters as much as the modules.
Which day the ice swim belongs on, how long a group can stay outside at minus twenty, and which evening to leave open.

