On April 26, 2016, Amber Jones, the mother of five children who were brutally murdered by her former husband, Timothy (Tim) Jones, Jr., in late August of 2014, filed a wrongful death suit against the state of South Carolina and the Lexington County Department of Social Services (DSS) for the deaths of her children.
The lawsuit alleges that DSS did not do enough to protect her children: Abigail, 1, Gabriel 2, Nathan, 6, Elias, 7 and Merah, 8, by placing them in their father’s care. The lawsuit reports that Tim was a “well-documented child abuser” (2) and provides a timeline of reported investigations that began in 2011 following reports of neglect and “substantial risk of physical injury.” (2) In 2013 and 2014, the children’s school filed reports with DSS; one of which was a report that Tim choked one of the children and threw one against the wall. A babysitter made a report of abuse in 2014. DSS reportedly showed negligence in 11 areas and only created safety plans in response to the investigations.
Following the murders in late August 2014, Tim was reported to be under the influence of drugs and believed his children were going “chop him up and feed him to the dogs.” (2) Tim allegedly strangled the children to death in his home, placed them in plastic bags, put them in his vehicle, and drove around with them for six days prior to dumping their bodies in rural Alabama. On September 11, 2014, he stopped at a traffic checkpoint in Mississippi and was taken into custody due to blood on the interior and the smell of death coming from the vehicle. Tim is currently being held in Lexington County, SC where he waits to stand trial for five counts of murder in the deaths of his five children.
The lawsuit states, “Each child suffer[ed] a horrific, but entirely preventable death.” (1) DSS was reported to be knowledgeable of the risks the children were in from their father and Amber is seeking damages for the “wrongful deaths and conscious pain and suffering of her children.” (2)

Nova 3D Whale4 Ultra 16K Resin 3D Printer
- 10-inch 16K Exquisite Details 15120*6230 Resolution
- 14×19µm XY Resolution
- Build volume of 211.68 x 118.37*220mm³
- Sealed Z-axis system，12mm lead screw + Dual Limit Switch Design
- Equipped with Gorilla LCD protector, fearless about resin residues. The small resin won’t cause damage to your LCD
- One-step leveling design
- Advanced #6 Gen COB lights engine
- Resin Heating System + Air Purifier
- Hover Flip Cover Design
- NOVAMAKER Intelligent Control System
Share:
The Nova 3D Whale4 Ultra 16K Resin 3D Printer is a high-resolution LCD resin 3D printer built for users who want exceptional detail, a generous build area, and efficient printing performance. With a 15120 × 6230 resolution, 14 × 19 μm pixel size, and 221 × 118 × 220 mm build volume, the Whale4 Ultra is designed for both detailed models and larger resin printing projects.
Its 16K monochrome LCD provides a high level of detail, while the increased 220 mm build height gives users more freedom when printing taller models. Combined with a rated printing speed of up to 100 mm/h, the Whale4 Ultra offers a strong balance between print quality, size, and productivity.
Key Features of Nova 3D Whale4 Ultra
16K Resolution for Exceptional Detail
The Whale4 Ultra features a 15120 × 6230 resolution display with a 14 × 19 μm pixel size.
This high-resolution printing system is designed to reproduce fine edges, intricate textures, small features, and detailed surface geometry. It makes the printer suitable for users who want smooth and highly detailed resin prints.
For miniature models, prototypes, figurines, decorative parts, and other detailed projects, the 16K resolution provides the level of precision expected from a modern high-resolution resin 3D printer.
Large Build Volume for Bigger Models
With a 221 × 118 × 220 mm build volume, the Nova 3D Whale4 Ultra provides substantial printing space across all three axes.
The 220 mm Z-axis height is particularly useful for taller models and larger components. The additional build space also allows users to arrange multiple smaller parts within the same print.
This makes the Whale4 Ultra a versatile option for both individual large models and batch printing.
Fast Resin 3D Printing
The Whale4 Ultra supports a rated printing speed of up to 100 mm/h.
This gives users the ability to complete suitable projects more efficiently while maintaining the advantages of high-resolution resin printing.
Actual print speed will depend on resin type, layer thickness, exposure settings, model geometry, and slicing parameters.
Advanced COB UV Light Source
The printer uses a 7th-generation COB light source with a light homogenizer and an integrated air-cooling system.
Its optical power intensity is rated at 5000 μW/cm², with a 405nm UV wavelength.
The light homogenizing system helps provide consistent exposure across the printing area. This is important for maintaining reliable curing and consistent detail across different areas of the build platform.
Stable Industrial Motion System
The Whale4 Ultra uses an industrial ball screw and industrial stepper motor for its motion system.
A stable Z-axis is important for resin printing because each layer needs to be positioned accurately during the build process. The industrial motion components help provide controlled vertical movement throughout the print.
Flexible Layer Thickness
The Nova 3D Whale4 Ultra supports layer thicknesses from 20 μm to 200 μm, with 20 μm increments.
Users can select finer layers when prioritizing surface quality and detail. Thicker layers can be selected for suitable models when printing efficiency is more important.
This flexibility allows the printer to adapt to different model sizes and printing requirements.
Suitable for a Wide Range of Applications
Unlike printers designed specifically around one professional industry, the Whale4 Ultra works well as a general-purpose high-resolution resin 3D printer.
It can be used for applications such as:
- Miniature and collectible models
- Figurines and character models
- Product prototypes
- Engineering prototypes
- Artistic and decorative models
- Small functional components
- Detailed design models
- Larger resin prints
- Small-batch production
The printer’s larger build volume also makes it useful when several smaller models need to be printed together.
Designed for Larger Resin Projects
The Whale4 Ultra’s 220 mm build height gives it an advantage when working with taller models.
Many resin printers focus heavily on XY resolution, but available Z-axis space can become a limitation for larger designs. The Whale4 Ultra provides additional vertical capacity while maintaining its high-resolution 16K printing system.
This makes it a practical choice for users who regularly print both highly detailed and relatively large resin models.
Easy Resin Printing Workflow
The printer supports several widely used resin slicing platforms, including NovaMaker, Chitubox, Lychee Slicer, and Tango Slicer.
Models can be prepared using common STL and OBJ file formats, making it easier to integrate the Whale4 Ultra into existing 3D modeling and resin printing workflows.
A Versatile Professional Resin 3D Printer
The Nova 3D Whale4 Ultra 16K combines high resolution with a larger build volume and faster rated printing speed.
Its 15120 × 6230 resolution is suited to detailed models, while the 221 × 118 × 220 mm build area provides room for larger projects and multi-model printing.
For designers, makers, model creators, prototyping businesses, and professional users, the Whale4 Ultra provides a versatile platform for high-detail resin 3D printing.
Why Choose the Nova 3D Whale4 Ultra?
The main advantage of the Nova 3D Whale4 Ultra resin 3D printer is its combination of 16K resolution, large build volume, and up to 100 mm/h printing speed.
Instead of choosing between detail and printing capacity, users get a machine designed to handle both. The high-resolution LCD is suitable for intricate models, while the 220 mm build height provides additional flexibility for larger designs.
If you need a high-resolution resin 3D printer for detailed models, prototypes, miniatures, and larger resin prints, the Whale4 Ultra is a strong option for professional and advanced users.
Nova 3D Whale4 Ultra Specifications
| Specification | Details | 
| Light Source | 7th-gen COB + Light Homogenizer | 
| Cooling | 4th-gen Integrated Air-Cooling System | 
| Optical Power | 5000 μW/cm² | 
