Positioned on one of Carlton North’s most recognisable thoroughfares, this substantial period residence offers the scale, flexibility and land component that continue to attract family buyers to Melbourne’s inner north. The wider frontage creates a strong street presence, while the generous accommodation provides versatility for families at different stages of life. Its proximity to Rathdowne Village, Princes Park, schools, transport and the CBD further enhances long-term owner-occupier appeal and supports ongoing demand for quality homes in the area.
The primary compromise is the Station Street location, which introduces higher levels of traffic, noise and activity compared to quieter residential streets nearby. Some buyers may also identify opportunities for further cosmetic improvement or modernisation depending on their requirements. Comparable sales within a similar price range have generally included larger period homes in Carlton North and Princes Hill that offer flexible family accommodation but may not occupy the area's most tightly held residential streets. This positioning is likely to attract buyers seeking a balance between land size, accommodation and value within a blue-chip inner north location.
Sales at 105 Lee St Carlton at $2,000,000 and 256 Rae St, Fitzroy North at $2,000,000 also support the "spot on" quote rnage
