In this first episode of the World Bank Group's Trade Tips podcast, we explore why trade matters and how it benefits economies all over the globe. We learn about the big picture when it comes to trade and how it can be made more efficient for traders. We hear from traders in Nepal and Tonga about their challenges, and from the World Bank Group's Mona Haddad, Director of Trade, Investment, and Competitiveness, on possible solutions. Listen now! Tell us what you think of our podcast here. Featured VoicesSundar Dahal, owner, Starlight Express, Nepal: “We should have our own exports, rather than the assembled ones. So, I thought we should start exporting tea, coffee, turmeric, ginger.”Tai’atu Ataata, owner of JJ Rose Store and Gallery, Tonga: “You have to have that go get attitude because it’s difficult to operate. You just have to pull yourself up and keep going.”Mona Haddad, Director of Trade, Investment, and Competitiveness, World Bank Group: "Trade is an engine of growth that creates better jobs, reduces poverty, and increases economic opportunity. Economic growth underlined by better trade practices, has lifted more than one billion people out of poverty since 1990.” Timestamps[00:02] Welcome and introduction [01:27] Perspective from a cardamon trader in Nepal [05:06] From landlocked Nepal to the Pacific island nation of Tonga [08:09] Now to Washington: Why is efficient and smooth trade so important for economies? [09:45] What is trade facilitation? [10:37] Where does the World Bank Group play a role? [11:58] Closing and thanks for listening! Presenter and Producer: Sarah Treanor Executive Producer: Marisa Zawacki *** This podcast was created by the World Bank Group with funding from Trade Facilitation Support Program (TFSP). The TFSP is funded by nine donor partners: Australia, Canada, the European Commission, the Netherlands, Norway, Sweden, Switzerland, the United States, and the United Kingdom. This initiative provides assistance to countries seeking to align their trade practices with the World Trade Organization Trade Facilitation Agreement (WTO TFA). *** ABOUT THE TRADE TIPS PODCASTThis Trade Tips podcast tackles the big issues in the world of trade and explores solutions. In this new podcast from the World Bank Group, we take you on a journey around the globe – from Vanuatu to Ghana, Jamaica to Nepal, London to Washington, DC. Through conversations with traders who are being affected by key issues like climate change, digitization, gender – and experts offering cutting-edge solutions – we highlight why trade matters and how it can be made more efficient. Don't miss an episode! a href="https://trade-tips-world-bank-group.captivate.fm/listen"

Seedream AI Studio
Generate images with Seedream 5.0 and turn selected results into short videos in one browser workflow.
AI tool Details
About Seedream AI Studio
Seedream AI Studio is an independent browser-based creative tool for generating images with current Seedream models, comparing outputs across versions, and turning selected images into short videos. It is built by ByteDance and wraps every current Seedream version: Seedream 5.0, Seedream 5.0 Lite, Seedream 4.5, and Seedream 4.0. The tool also integrates Kling 2.1 for image-to-video animation, allowing creators to move from prompt to image to video in one seamless workflow without leaving the page. Seedream AI Studio is designed for e-commerce brands, content creators, marketers, and artists who need fast, high-quality visual production. Its main value proposition is offering a single platform where users can draft quickly on Seedream 5.0 Lite, balance quality and cost on Seedream 4.5, render hero shots on Seedream 5.0, or keep Seedream 4.0 for stylized art. The tool provides a free tier with 20 welcome credits for new accounts, valid for 2 days, so users can test all capabilities before committing. Image generation takes 12 to 30 seconds, and video animation produces 5 to 15 second clips. Seedream AI Studio supports natural-language image editing, character consistency, and photo-realistic quality, making it a powerful all-in-one solution for visual AI creation.
Multi-Model Image Generation
Choose from four distinct Seedream versions to match your creative needs. Seedream 5.0 delivers the highest fidelity for hero shots and production work. Seedream 5.0 Lite is the fastest and cheapest option, ideal for drafting and iteration. Seedream 4.5 offers the best balance of quality and cost, recommended for most production work with roughly 20-second generation times. Seedream 4.0 remains the favorite for stylized art and illustration. Each model generates images at 1K resolution by default, with support for multiple aspect ratios including 1:1, 16:9, 9:16, 3:2, 2:3, 5:4, 4:5, 4:3, and 3:4.
One-Click Image-to-Video Animation
Any generated image can be instantly animated into a 5 to 15 second video using Kling 2.1 technology. After generating an image, click the big "ANIMATE THIS" button to auto-fill the image into the video card on the right. Add a motion prompt and generate the video directly in the same interface. This eliminates the need to download, upload, or switch between different tools, saving time and keeping your creative flow uninterrupted.
Side-by-Side Version Comparison
Draft an image on Seedream 5.0 Lite, then re-run the same prompt on Seedream 4.5 or Seedream 4.0 to compare outputs directly. The browser-based interface allows you to see results from different models side by side, helping you choose the best version for your specific use case. This feature is particularly valuable for brands and creators who need to evaluate quality, style, and cost trade-offs before finalizing assets.
Image Editing and Variation Tools
After generating an image, you can edit the prompt, download in HD, or create variations with a single click. The tool supports natural-language image editing, meaning you can type instructions like "change the bikini to red" and the model applies the change intelligently. This makes it easy to refine visuals without starting from scratch, saving credits and time while maintaining character consistency and photo-realism.
E-Commerce Product Photography
E-commerce brands can generate high-fidelity product images using Seedream 5.0 for hero shots, then quickly animate them into short promotional videos with Kling 2.1. The ability to draft on Seedream 5.0 Lite and refine on Seedream 4.5 allows teams to iterate rapidly on product visuals, test different backgrounds, and create consistent image sets for listings, ads, and social media without hiring photographers or renting studios.
Social Media Content Creation
Content creators and social media managers can generate eye-catching images and animated clips in minutes. Use Seedream 4.0 for stylized art that stands out in feeds, or Seedream 4.5 for balanced quality on Instagram and TikTok. The one-click animation feature turns static posts into engaging short videos, increasing reach and engagement. The free tier with 20 credits lets creators test concepts before investing in paid credits.
Brand and Marketing Asset Production
Marketing teams can produce consistent visual assets across campaigns using the character consistency and natural-language editing features of Seedream models. Generate multiple variations of the same prompt across different Seedream versions to find the perfect style for each channel. Animate key images into video ads or social media stories directly in the tool, streamlining the entire asset creation pipeline from concept to final output.
Illustration and Concept Art
Artists and designers can leverage Seedream 4.0 for stylized illustration work, then use Seedream 5.0 for high-detail concept art. The ability to compare outputs across versions helps artists explore different aesthetic directions quickly. Image-to-video animation adds motion to static concepts, useful for storyboarding, presentation mockups, or portfolio pieces. The tool's resolution options and aspect ratio flexibility support various output formats for different projects.
Frequently Asked Questions
What Seedream models are available in Seedream AI Studio?
Seedream AI Studio includes four current Seedream models: Seedream 5.0 (highest fidelity, best for hero shots), Seedream 5.0 Lite (fastest and cheapest, ideal for drafting), Seedream 4.5 (best balance of quality and cost, recommended for most production work), and Seedream 4.0 (favorite for stylized art and illustration). Each model generates images in 12 to 30 seconds and supports multiple aspect ratios at 1K resolution.
How does the image-to-video animation feature work?
After generating an image using any Seedream model, click the "ANIMATE THIS" button on the result. The image auto-fills into the video card on the right side of the interface. You can add a motion prompt and generate a 5 to 15 second video using Kling 2.1 technology. The entire process happens within the same page without downloading or uploading files, making it fast and seamless.
What is the pricing and credit system?
Seedream AI Studio offers a free tier where new accounts receive 20 welcome credits, valid for 2 days. Image generation costs 2 credits per image. Video generation costs 15 credits per video. Users can buy additional credits as needed. There is no monthly subscription requirement, and you only pay for what you generate. The free credits allow you to test all models and the animation feature before purchasing.
Can I edit images after generation?
Yes, you can edit images after generation using natural-language commands. After generating an image, you have options to download in HD, edit the prompt, or create variations. The natural-language editing feature allows you to type instructions like "change the bikini to red" and the model applies the change intelligently. This enables quick refinements without regenerating from scratch, saving credits and time.
