STAN'S OCTOBER HIGHLIGHTS
What everyone will be talking about next month
All Episodes At Once
Senior Sergeant Arnold Kipps (Asa Butterfield) is having a totally sub-par day in suburbia. His ex-partner and ex-flame Ellie McKay (Megan Smart) has just returned to Nompton to shut down his police station, right when an ancient, evil force is awakened by the bloodthirsty Gnome Queen. Unleashing a nightmare horde of killer ceramic gnomes upon the unsuspecting town, Nompton is instantly plunged into pure, unadulterated chaos.
Armed with an array of unconventional weapons and sheer desperation, Arnold and Ellie must reunite a ragtag team of misfit cops, rebellious teens, and an overly ambitious mayor to stop the Gnome Queen’s rampage before the entire town gets dug up from the roots. Because these lawn ornaments aren't just angry, they’re out to smash faces and take names.
Gnomes stars Asa Butterfield (Sex Education) alongside beloved Australian stars Megan Smart (Class of '07), Matt Okine (Mother and Son, Stan Original The Other Guy), and Luke McGregor (Utopia).
From A24 and the executive producer of IT: Welcome to Derry comes Crystal Lake, the gripping prequel within the infamous world of Friday the 13th. The series stars 2026 Emmy® Winner Linda Cardellini (DTF St. Louis, Dead to Me) as Pam Voorhees, a grieving single mother unable to move on from the tragic drowning of her son, Jason, in the local town lake. Pam’s elusive past resurfaces, however, when two probing strangers arrive at her door, setting alight a disturbing chain of events that leaves the townspeople of Crystal Lake wondering: who is Pam Voorhees?
Starring Academy Award®, BAFTA, and Tony Award-winning actress Catherine Zeta-Jones (Chicago, Wednesday), Kill Jackie is the thrilling new revenge series based on the acclaimed novel The Price You Pay from Sunday Times best-selling author Nick Harkaway.
Jackie has been living a luxurious existence for the last twenty years – travelling the world, selling fine art and, above all, trying to stay anonymous after escaping a dangerous past as an international drug smuggler. But just as life starts to feel a little boring, it takes a sudden lethal turn when she discovers that The Seven Demons, a squad of the world’s most terrifying hitmen, have been hired to kill her.
From the creatives behind Killing Eve and Gangs of London, Kill Jackie is co-produced by Australia-based Steel Springs Pictures and Fremantle, with Australian filmmaker Peter Lawson (John Wick) as co-creator and executive producer.
Appearing alongside Zeta-Jones is Daniel Ings (A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms), Sidse Babett Knudsen (Borgen), Óscar Jaenada (Rambo V, Cantinflas), Darci Shaw (A Thousand Blows), Raff Law (Masters of The Air), and Australian actress Hattie Hook (Stan Original Ten Pound Poms).
Love Island Australia is getting an exclusive series on Stan. Audiences will have access to more Love Island than ever before, with a daily drop of unseen and uncut feeds direct from the Villa, as audiences get VIP access to the Islanders. Think they've been clipped to look a certain way? See for yourself. It's real villa life in real time, unfiltered and unpredictable.
New Episodes Every Saturday
Based on the best-selling novel by John Grisham, The Rainmaker follows new lawyer Rudy Baylor as he goes head-to-head with courtroom lion Leo Drummond. The new season explores a case where the lives of hundreds of children are uncertain - a case where winning may be just as dangerous as losing.
Starring John Slattery (Mad Men) and Milo Callaghan (Dune: Prophecy), the upcoming season welcomes new cast members Merle Dandridge and Richard Kind.
The hit crime drama This City Is Ours follows Michael (James Nelson-Joyce) who is caught in a ruthless power struggle over the Phelan family’s underworld empire.
The new season picks up with Michael and Diana (Hannah Onslow) having barely settled in Spain, before being dragged back into questioning around Ricardo’s death. Meanwhile in Liverpool, internal tensions continue to rise among the remaining gang members, with new threats arising from an old school gangster from Ronnie’s era. The upcoming season will see new cast members Shaun Evans (Until I Kill You, Endeavour) and Álvaro Morte (Money Heist, Immaculate, The Wheel of Time).
New True Crime Series
Unravelling a real-life psychological thriller about extreme teenage jealousy and toxic family dynamics, this documentary explores the murder of 16-year-old Becky Watts. When Becky vanished from her home, the huge search for her became national news. But as the investigation closed in, the mask of the ‘perfect family life’ began to slip, revealing a dark obsession and a monster hiding in plain sight. Combining the intimacy of the teenage relationships at the heart of the story—told firsthand by Becky’s friends—with the experience of the police officers who worked the case, it reveals what happens when the killers aren’t strangers, but people shockingly close to home.
In July 2010, Raoul Moat went on a two-day shooting spree, killing one person and seriously injuring two others. In a terrifying rampage, Raoul Moat led police on a week-long manhunt across the Northeast of England, leaving the country in fear of when he may strike next. Fifteen years after police deployed an unprecedented, large-scale manhunt, Raoul Moat: Inside the Mind of a Killer follows the legacy of these events.
Continue streaming all your Stan favourites in October: Outlander: Blood of my Blood season 2, Survivor season 51, Universal Basic Guys season 3, RuPaul's Drag Race UK season 8, and American Hostage season 1.
'Tis the season for screams, spells, and spooky cinematic thrills. Watch these horror films coming this October, including: Speak No Evil (2024), The Watchers (2024), A Quiet Place Part II, The Nun 2, The Grudge (2020), and Hostel (2006).
October is loaded with more must-watch TV to dive into on Stan including: Seinfeld, Sex and the City seasons 1-6, I, Jack Wright season 1, Blue Lights season 3, Stock, Aitken & Waterman season 1, Around the World in 80 Days (2021) season 1, Mushoku Tensei: Jobless Reincarnation season 1, The Sonny Disposition season 1, and Ballers seasons 1-5.
Grab the popcorn and press play on these blockbuster films landing across October including: Power Ballad, The Colour Purple (2024), The Order, Holland, Killer Heat, and Here's Hoges.
Stan is your one-stop destination for entertainment the whole family can enjoy, with countless hours of viewing for kids of all ages. October will see The Wild Robot and Power Rangers: Beast Morphers land on Stan.
