The great in The Great Gatsby: A lesson in 1920s fashion
This article has been researched and written by Samrat Amarnani. AI has not been used in producing this article.
The 2013 Hollywood film The Great Gatsby, starring Leonardo DiCaprio, not only received critical acclaim but also reignited global interest in the elegance and extravagance of 1920s fashion. The film serves as a visual masterclass in vintage style, showcasing how classic tailoring, luxurious fabrics, and refined details can create unforgettable looks.
For those looking to introduce a touch of old-world charm into their wardrobe, the film offers endless inspiration. At Collars & Cuffs, we specialise in recreating these timeless aesthetics through bespoke tailoring, allowing you to channel vintage sophistication with a modern edge.
The 1920s, famously known as the decade of decadence, were a mystical era that featured the swing, social revolution, and most importantly, elaborate parties and outfits. Jay Gatsby, effortlessly portrays himself in this unforgettable scene in an ivory colored suit, with a point and eyelet collar silk gray shirt and tobacco brown contrast waistcoat. His look is completed with a striped yellow tie and sunburst cufflinks that bring it all together
One of the movie’s most iconic looks is this three-piece single breasted pink linen suit, also featured in the 1974 film adaptation worn by Robert Redford, which famously symbolized the love Jay Gatsby had for Daisy and his hope for them being together again. This soft linen fabric features a stunning yet subtle widely-spaced white pinstripe. He pairs his look with a classic eyelet collar shirt and continues the pink into his silk tie, consisting of thick burgundy and salmon stripes.
It mustn’t be easy playing a supporting role to a well-dressed millionaire, but Nick Carraway (Tobey Maguire) has done so dapperly in his vintage suits, such as this stunning brown herringbone three piece look straight out of the Jazz era featuring a distinctive patch pocket with a slit. He appears elegant and perfectly accessorized with his diagonally-striped tie and unique watch chain draped from one waistcoat pocket to the next and attached to the center waistcoat button.
Tom Buchanan brings a commanding presence to the screen, reflected in his powerful wardrobe choices. His double-breasted suit, featuring peak lapels and a high-fitting waistcoat, creates a strong, authoritative silhouette. This look is characterised by its sharp structure — from the wide lapels to the minimal shirt exposure, revealing only the knot of the tie. Paired with a pointed collar shirt and classic cufflinks, the ensemble exudes confidence and dominance. It’s a reminder that tailoring is not just about style — it’s also about attitude and presence.
The enduring appeal of 1920s fashion lies in its attention to detail, luxurious fabrics, and impeccable tailoring. Whether you prefer bold statement pieces or understated elegance, these iconic looks can be adapted to suit modern tastes while retaining their vintage charm.
Inspired by the film and looking to recreate a classic bespoke suit or a refined vintage shirt? Collars & Cuffs can bring your vision to life with expert craftsmanship and personalised design.
For more information, call +971 4 333 7848 | +971 55 497 4342 or email <EMAIL>

Pakistan Certificate Attestation is the process of verifying a Pakistani document for official use in the UAE. In general, it helps confirm the authenticity of the document, signatures, stamps, and issuing authority. Depending on the type of document, the process may first involve HEC or IBCC verification. After that, the document may need Pakistan MOFA attestation, followed by UAE Embassy attestation. Finally, it may require UAE MOFA attestation before it can be submitted to the relevant authority in the UAE.
You may need this service for a degree, diploma, school certificate, birth certificate, marriage certificate, Nikah Nama, experience certificate, PCC, medical document, commercial document, or Power of Attorney. Since every document can have different requirements, checking the correct attestation route before starting can help prevent avoidable delays. With 30+ years of experience, Best Legal Consultancy reviews your document, explains the required stages, and assists you throughout the attestation process.
Pakistani documents may need authentication before UAE authorities can accept them for official use. In general, attestation helps confirm that a document comes from a recognised issuing authority. Therefore, completing the required attestation steps can help avoid delays during official applications.
For example, a Pakistani university degree normally needs HEC attestation before moving to the later authentication stages. Similarly, school and intermediate certificates may have different requirements through IBCC or the relevant education authority. As a result, the required process can vary based on the type of document and its purpose.
In particular, people commonly need Pakistani document attestation for:
However, the exact requirements depend on the document, issuing authority, and UAE authority requesting it. For this reason, checking the required authentication stages before starting the process can help prevent unnecessary delays or document issues.
Our assistance can include:
The team first reviews the document and explains the required stages. This helps you understand what needs to happen before submission.
The process can vary based on the document. However, a common route includes the following stages.
Start with the original Pakistani document. The issuing authority, document type, spelling, signatures, and supporting documents should be checked before submission.
Educational documents may need verification from HEC, IBCC, or another relevant authority. For example, the UAE Embassy in Islamabad states that bachelor, master, and PhD degrees require prior HEC and Pakistan MOFA attestation.
The document may then need attestation from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Pakistan. Pakistan’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs states that Pakistani documents require the relevant MOFA authentication before embassy level attestation.
The next stage can involve UAE Embassy attestation in Pakistan. The UAE Embassy in Islamabad provides document attestation services for eligible Pakistani documents after the required Pakistani authentication stages.
The final UAE stage is UAE MOFA attestation. The UAE Ministry of Foreign Affairs states that attestation certifies the authenticity of signatures and seals on documents.
The current UAE digital attestation service for Pakistan issued documents can cover both UAE Embassy attestation in Islamabad and UAE MOFA attestation through one application for eligible documents.
The attestation route depends on the type of Pakistani document. A simple flow can help you understand the usual process:
University / Issuing Authority
Pakistan MOFA Attestation
UAE Embassy Attestation
UAE MOFA Attestation
School / Education Authority
IBCC Verification or Attestation
Relevant Pakistani Authority
Note: These are general routes. The required stages can vary based on the document, issuing authority, and purpose. Original documents should meet the applicable UAE MOFA requirements, and laminated documents are not accepted for attestation.
A small document error can cause delays. With 30+ years of experience, Best Legal Consultancy helps clients understand and manage the certificate attestation process based on their document and intended use.
Our support includes:
Simple process:
Document Review → Requirement Check → Pakistan MOFA → UAE Embassy → UAE MOFA → Document Return
Our team explains the required stages and helps you manage the process while avoiding common document-related mistakes.
Getting Pakistani documents attested for use in the UAE can involve several authorities and different requirements. A small mistake at any stage can lead to delays or additional document work.
With 30+ years of experience, Best Legal Consultancy assists clients with Pakistani certificate attestation for use in the UAE. Our team reviews your documents, explains the required process, and helps coordinate the necessary attestation stages.
We aim to make the attestation process easier to understand and manage. Our team can help you identify the required stages before processing begins and assist with the documents throughout the process.
If you need to attest a Pakistani document for use in the UAE, Best Legal Consultancy can assist you with the required process.
Contact us today to discuss your document attestation requirements.
