Example Visual Feng Shui Report
This is what a visfeng report looks like on a real bedroom photo: door line, bed zone, mirror reflection, window pressure, and what to fix first. No upload needed to preview the format.
Full sample: score, issues, and first fix
Same report structure you get after uploading your bedroom photo — layout score, top issues, annotated image, and the highest-impact fix first.
Top 3 Issues
- Command Position Violated Bed is directly in line with the door, which may create a sense of exposure and restlessness.
- Active Mirror Placement Mirror on the closet door faces the bed, potentially reflecting energy during restorative hours.
- Window Pressure Lack of solid backing behind the headboard weakens personal support and stability.
What to Fix First
Relocate the Bed to the Solid Wall
Moving the bed to the opposite wall establishes a solid backing and positions you to see the door without being directly in its path. This is the foundational step to securing restful energy.
