Orange Flag Towns of Campania
| Latest page update: 2 March 2025 | By: Dion Protani | 
| The Touring Club Italiano association have chosen four Orange Flag towns of Campania to represent the region. Across the country there are dozens of towns that have been awarded the Bandiera Arancione to signify their touristic merits.  Campania's selection includes the historic hill town of Sant'Agata de' Goti with its fascinating narrow streets just one part of its charm and the spectacular views as you approach it another. Cerreto Sannita is famous for its ceramics, some of the best examples of which are displayed on its town centre churches. |  | 
Both Letino and Zungoli have an air of mystique about them; they occupy areas of land that are decidedly off the beaten track and a delight to explore. 
Campania Top 10 - My Recommended Destinations in Campania
9. Royal Palace of Caserta
👉 Explore the Top 10 Places to Visit in Campania

