What is the average property management fee in Florida?
When searching for property management services in Florida, one of the most common questions property owners ask is, “What is the average property management fee in Florida?” Typically, property management companies in the state charge anywhere from 8% to 12% of the monthly rental income. This percentage can vary depending on the location, type of property, and the range of services included. Some managers may also offer flat-rate pricing, but percentage-based fees are the most common, as they scale with the rental income of the property.
In addition to the monthly management fee, property owners should be aware of other possible costs. These can include leasing fees for securing new tenants, renewal fees when tenants re-sign, and maintenance markups on repairs or vendor services. Understanding these fees upfront allows landlords to compare providers and ensure they’re getting the best value for their investment while keeping rental income optimized.

