Laos e-Visa requirements for Uruguayan citizens
Updated: January 25, 2024
Laos is the only landlocked ASEAN country and one of the world's least visited countries. Because it has been secluded for many years, Lao PDR has retained a wonderful peacefulness and timeless charm. Because of the country's rugged terrain, transport is challenging, with limited internal flights and adventurous navigation down the Mekong River. Vientiane, the capital, is a small (140.000) town that is attractive and picturesque, lying on the banks of the Mekong. It has some vibrant and sacred pagodas, great museums, large boulevards, and attractions such as Patuxai, and Vientiane's Arc de Triomphe.
Thanaleng is the location of the Thai border crossing and the Friendship Bridge. Budha Park in this town is an odd collection of concrete religious icons. Nam Ngum Dam, located on the city's northwestern outskirts, is a tranquil hideaway with restaurants, fishing, and tiny cabins. Luang Prabang, the historic capital, is one of ASEAN's most tranquil cities. A large portion of the town and its pagodas are designated as UNESCO World Heritage Sites. Within a short distance of one other, there are approximately 32 historic pagodas.
Laos e visa for Uruguayan citizens
Many native products, particularly those of the nearby hill tribe, are sold in the Dala market. Many Lao treasures can be found in the Royal Palace Museum. Mekong river cruises are popular, particularly to the Pak Ou limestone caverns, which contain hundreds of Buddhist images. For decades, archaeologists have been drawn to the Plain of Jars outside the little hamlet of Phonsavan.
The purpose of the massive 2,000-year-old stone jars is unknown. Pakse, in the country's south, is a starting place for trips to the Bolaven Plateau and the Khmer ruins at Wat Phu. The area is also well-known for its delicious coffee. The Mekong River's Khon Papheng Falls is a 13-kilometer series of rapids and cascades.
Laos' government allows people from more than 150 countries, including Uruguay, to apply for electronic travel authorization to visit the nation.
Before entering Laos, Uruguayan citizens must have a valid visa, which can be obtained in a variety of ways. The Laos eVisa Approval Letter, on the other hand, provides a rapid and effective manner of registering travelers to enter the nation.
Discover Laos visa requirements for Uruguayan citizens and how to apply online in a matter of minutes below.
1. Do Uruguayan Citizens Need a Visa for Laos?
Yes, a valid visa is required for Uruguayan nationals to visit Laos regardless of the purpose of their visit or the duration of their stay.
Now that you can only get a Laos tourist visa in Uruguay, you don't have to wait in a long line at the Laos border to apply for an arrival visa or visit the embassy or consulate to submit your visa application yourself.
Laos visas online for Uruguayan citizens allow a single 30-day stay in the country for tourism. It is also possible to extend the e-visa for an additional 30 days (60 days in total).
To visit the country for other reasons, such as business, job, or study, or for longer lengths of time, you must apply for a visa at a Laos embassy in Uruguay.
2. What is a Laos visa for Uruguayan citizens?
The Laos eVisa is an official document that allows you to enter Laos. There is no need to schedule an appointment or bring original documentation to the Embassy or Consular Office.
The Laos eVisa permits Uruguayan citizens to enter the country once and stay for a maximum of 30 days. If the traveler(s) wishes to renew their Laos eVisa for a longer period of time or requires numerous visits to the country, they can apply for a Laos tourist visa instead. To do so, however, the traveler must first visit a local Lao embassy or consulate.
A Laos eVisa has a validity of 60 days with a single entry. Because all visits are exclusively limited to tourism, you are NOT permitted to pursue paid labor or employment.
Laos e-Visa holders may enter the nation through one of the five main entry points. These are some examples:
- Wattay International Airport (Vientiane Capital)
- Lao-Thai Friendship Bridge I (Vientiane Capital)
- Luang Prabang International Airport (Luang Prabang Province)
- Lao-Thai Friendship Bridge II (Savanakhet Province)
- Pakse International Airport (Champasak Province)
3. Laos e visa requirements for Uruguayan citizens:
Laos e visa requirements for Uruguayan citizens
Applicants must meet only a few online Laos visa requirements for Uruguayan citizens. It is required to have the following:
- All Uruguayan citizens must have a valid passport in order to enter Laos. Please keep in mind that your passport must be valid for at least six months after your arrival in Laos. Your Laos visa application may be declined otherwise.
- All applicants must include a current passport-size digital photo (in JPEG or PNG format). Please make sure the photo has a white/ plain background.
- An active email address: It is critical that the applicant supply an email address that they check frequently because the approved eVisa will be sent to this address.
- Means of payment – payments are online: debit or credit cards, Visa, Master Card, Amex, PayPal, or wire transfers to our bank account
In order to apply for a Laos visa from Uruguay, applicants must also have the following information on hand when completing the e-Visa application:
- Personal data (full name, gender, address, date of birth)
- Passport details (number, nationality.)
- Travel information (date of arrival and departure in Laos).
4. How to apply for a Laos visa online from Uruguay:
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Uruguay recently introduced the Tourist e-Visa for citizens of more than 150 countries. This Tourist e-Visa permits visitors to enter the nation for recreational activities. The Laos Tourist e-Visa application process is straightforward and entirely online. When the application is filled and accepted, the applicant will be issued an electronic visa, which must be presented to immigration officers upon arrival. Yes, it's that easy.
The eVisa system allows you to apply for a Laos visa online from anywhere in the world. The traveler benefits from this method in that visas can be applied for swiftly over the Internet at any time and from any location, and payment is completed online at the time of application.
Uruguayan travelers can get an online Laos visa from Uruguay in 3 simple steps:
- Fill out the easy Laos e-Visa application form. Fill in the blanks with basic personal, passport, and travel information. Most folks spend about 10-15 minutes completing the form.
- Confirm the tourist visa charge for Laos. To submit the application for processing, you must pay the e-Visa fee with a valid credit or debit card. After that, please send us some required documents to fully complete the application process.
- Receive the approved Laos visa for Uruguayan citizens through email. The passenger can then print a copy to bring with them and present upon arrival.
Before submitting the request, applicants should double-check that all of the information provided is correct. Errors may create processing delays and affect travel arrangements from Uruguay to Laos.
All notifications, including the Laos eVisa Approval Letter, are delivered to the supplied email address.
How Long Does It Take to Process the Laos eVisa from Uruguay?
The online procedure makes it simple to obtain a visa for Laos from Uruguay. The electronic visa application form takes only a few minutes to complete.
Visa processing is likewise quick and easy. The eVisa Approval Letter is usually emailed to Uruguayan citizens within 3 working days
What happens after I have applied?
After submitting your application, all you have to do is wait for your Laos Tourist eVisa to be emailed to you within the timeframe you choose. There is no need to engage with the embassy. We do it for you so you don't waste time. When you enter Laos, simply present a printed version of your Tourist eVisa together with your passport.
5. Laos e visa fees for Uruguayan citizens:
Laos e visa fees for Uruguayan citizens
The Laos e-visa fees will vary depending on how quickly you need your visa and your travel budget. The good news is that any of the possibilities will be relatively quick with Global Visa Services. They are as follows:
- Normal: your e-Visa will arrive by email within 3 Business Days
- Urgent: your e-Visa will be ready in your email inbox within 2 Business Days
- Super urgent: you’ll get the document in 1 Business Day
In addition, we recommend that you should buy Laos travel insurance. Travel insurance covers the costs, damages, and other expenses associated with travel. It protects policyholders against several types of damages that may occur when traveling. It includes a variety of services such as baggage/passport loss, flight delays, travel cancellations, medical expenditures, and so on. Every time you travel, your travel insurance serves as a safety net.
6. Is it safe to use Global Visa Services?
Yes, for sure. You can rely on our services. We've taken stringent efforts to ensure that no information you provide us is leaked. In addition, we have a high-performance team that will be in charge of accurately processing your Laos eVisa. In this manner, you can get it quickly and easily.
You can read what other clients think about us, which may help you decide whether to complete your eVisa with us.
7. Where can I get more information about the Laos e-visa for Uruguayan citizens?
To learn other useful information about the Laos eVisa for citizens of Uruguay, you can read more about A Guide To Obtaining Laos Tourist Visas
Remember that you can always return to our website to learn more about travel documents from around the world.
You can also contact us via online chat.

