A More Biologic Approach to Supporting Oral Health
At Smart Dentistry, we believe dental care should do more than treat what is visible. It should support the body, respect healthy tissues, and help create an environment where healing can happen more naturally.
That is one of the reasons we use ozone therapy in our practice.
Ozone is a highly energized form of oxygen that has been used in dentistry in different forms, including gas, water, and ozonated oils. In holistic dental care, it is valued for its ability to support a cleaner oral environment and to complement procedures in a way that is more biologically minded. Reviews of the dental literature describe ozone as being used across restorative care, periodontal therapy, endodontics, oral surgery, and management of certain oral lesions.
Why We Use Ozone in Our Practice
In a holistic practice, we are always asking a deeper question:
How can we support health, not just manage symptoms?
Ozone fits beautifully into that philosophy because it is often used as an adjunctive therapy something that works alongside high quality dental treatment to help reduce microbial burden and support healthier tissues. Current reviews consistently describe its best supported role in dentistry as a complementary tool rather than a replacement for proper diagnosis and treatment.
How Ozone May Be Used in Dental Care For periodontal therapy and gum health
Healthy gums are essential to a healthy body. When gum tissues are inflamed or affected by periodontal disease, our goal is not only to clean the area, but also to support a healthier environment for healing.
Ozone has been widely discussed in dentistry for its antimicrobial action and its role in periodontal care. Research reviews report that it has been used as an adjunct in periodontal treatment to help reduce harmful microbes and support tissue response when combined with conventional therapy.
For extractions and surgical procedures
When a tooth needs to be removed, we want to support the area as gently and thoroughly as possible. Ozone may be used as part of surgical care to help cleanse the treatment site and support the body’s healing response after the procedure. Reviews describe its use in dental surgery to help limit bacterial growth and support postoperative healing.
For cavities and restorative care
In holistic dentistry, preserving healthy tooth structure is always important. Ozone has been explored in cavity management because of its ability to help reduce bacterial activity in certain situations. The literature describes ozone as a promising tool in caries management, particularly as part of a conservative approach, though its use depends on the specific condition of the tooth and is not a substitute for restorative treatment when decay has progressed.
For root canal support and infected areas
Ozone has also been studied in endodontic care because of its antimicrobial properties. In some cases, it may be used to complement treatment in areas where reducing microbial load is especially important. Reviews of the evidence describe ozone as being investigated as an adjunct in endodontics, with some studies reporting reduced post treatment discomfort.
For oral tissues and comfort
Because ozone has been used in soft tissue and oral lesion care, it may also be helpful in selected situations where we want to support tissue health and comfort in a gentle, biologically supportive way. Published reviews describe potential applications for oral lesions and soft tissue healing, while also noting that research is still evolving.
A Supportive Tool, Not a Shortcut
One of the most important things patients should understand is that ozone is not a magic fix. In our practice, we do not present it that way.
Ozone is a supportive tool. It may help create a healthier environment, reduce microbial stress, and complement treatment, but it works best when it is part of a thoughtful, comprehensive plan. The current literature repeatedly describes ozone in dentistry as promising, but also emphasizes that evidence varies by use and that it is most often used alongside standard clinical care.
That is exactly how we approach it at Smart Dentistry.
Why It Belongs in a Holistic Practice
As a holistic dental office in Ocala, Florida, we believe the mouth is deeply connected to the rest of the body. What happens in the oral environment can influence inflammation, comfort, immune burden, and overall wellness.
That is why every decision matters.
The materials we use matter.
The techniques we choose matter.
The way we support healing matters.
Ozone therapy is one more way we align advanced dental care with a more natural and biologically respectful philosophy always with the goal of helping our patients feel healthier, safer, and more confident in their care.
A More Thoughtful Way to Care for Your Smile
At Smart Dentistry, we combine modern tools with a holistic mindset so patients can experience care that is more complete, more intentional, and more supportive of long term wellness.
Whether ozone is used as part of periodontal therapy, surgical care, restorative treatment, or tissue support, our purpose is always the same:
to provide care that looks beyond the tooth and considers the whole person.
If you are looking for a more natural, more comprehensive approach to dental care, we invite you to experience holistic dentistry at Smart Dentistry.
Here is a shorter luxury style version you could also use for a section on the page:
Ozone Therapy at Smart Dentistry
At Smart Dentistry, we believe truly holistic dental care should support the body’s natural balance whenever possible. That is why ozone therapy is one of the biologically minded tools we may incorporate into treatment.
Used in selected areas of dentistry such as gum therapy, surgical care, restorative support, and tissue management, ozone is valued for its ability to help reduce microbial burden and support a healthier oral environment. The dental literature most often describes it as an adjunctive therapy something that complements quality clinical care rather than replaces it.
For our patients, that means a more thoughtful approach one that looks beyond symptoms alone and considers healing, tissue health, and the connection between the mouth and the rest of the body. Reviews of current evidence describe ozone as promising in areas such as periodontal care, oral surgery, and selected restorative and endodontic applications, while also noting that its role continues to develop as research grows.
At our Ocala practice, we use every tool with intention. Ozone is no exception. It is part of our commitment to care that is advanced, gentle, and aligned with whole body wellness.
