 What is a proxy?
Simply put, a proxy is a device connected to the internet with its own IP address. It works as an intermediary between you and the rest of the internet. A proxy handles all your requests and keeps your IP concealed while providing various other useful functions along with privacy and security benefits depending on your needs.
 How to use Niger proxy?
A proxy server doesn’t just keep your private information safe. Niger proxies feature all sorts of options for different types of users. Companies can benefit from anonymous data scraping, global ad verification, and improved corporate privacy. Home users have the option to restrict access to specific content types and enjoy better deals on goods and services online.
 What is an SSL/HTTPs proxy?
SSL proxies are a transparent proxy type that enforces Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) encryption and decryption of traffic between clients and servers. Both the server and the client are unable to detect its presence. HTTPs proxies ensure communication between the client and the server with end-to-end security by establishing a secure channel for requests and returning information.
 What is a residential proxy?
A residential proxy uses an IP address assigned to a device by an internet service provider (ISP) along with its physical location. A residential proxy replaces your IP address with its own, hiding your identity online and maintaining your anonymity. They’re a perfect choice for web scraping, ad verification, and other scenarios where preserving your anonymity is a must.

Simon & Garfunkel Through the Years
Simon & Garfunkel Through the Years is a celebrated live tribute show recreating the iconic duo’s timeless music, harmonies and story.
Seventh Avenue Arts presents: Simon & Garfunkel Through the Years, an internationally acclaimed theatre show celebrating the music and legacy of one of the greatest duos in popular music history. Touring worldwide for over 15 years, the production has earned standing ovations across the UK, Europe and beyond for its faithful recreation of the unmistakable Simon & Garfunkel sound.
Performed by lifelong friends Dan Haynes and Pete Richards, the show captures the close harmonies, intricate guitar work and timeless songwriting behind classics including The Sound of Silence, Mrs Robinson, The Boxer and Bridge Over Troubled Water.
More than a traditional tribute, this moving live concert takes audiences on a journey through songs and history of Simon & Garfunkel, keeping their music alive for new generations while delighting devoted fans worldwide.
“A masterpiece”- BBC Radio
“One of the greatest tribute shows anywhere in the world” - Stuart Cameron, BBC and ITV Broadcaster.
