Jun 27, 2014
Ronnie from OH Asked Note: This answer was provided prior to the change to planDisney and may still contain references to Disney Parks Moms Panel.
Experiences, policies, pricing and other offerings are subject to change and may have changed since the date of this answer. What is the quickest way to travel from AK to Hollywood around 2pm and then back to AK around 6 or 7pm for dinner? What is the quickest way to travel from MK to Hollywood? After Fantasmic, is the boat ride the quickest back to Old Key West? If not, w Hi Ronnie,
There is a bus that runs between Animal Kingdom and Disney's Hollywood Studios, but I'm not sure it's the "quickest" method. If you don't have a personal car, and aren't interested in a taxi, the bus is your only option between those two parks. Be sure to give yourself a good window of time for traveling between parks and resorts. When you are figuring out how much time you will need to travel between parks and resorts there are a few things you need to remember.
  - How long it takes to get to the bus stop. Whether this is from your hotel room or from the back of a park, it will take time to get to the stop.
  - Buses run approximately every twenty minutes. Sometimes the timing is a bit off and there is always the possibility of arriving at the bus stop only to see your desired bus driving off (always a heart breaking moment!)
  - How long it will take to get to your desired destination from where you arrive. Whether you are traveling to a park, resort, or dining reservation, it will take time to walk from the bus stop to your destination.
From the Magic Kingdom park to Disney's Hollywood Studios, you will need to take the monorail or ferry back to the Ticket and Transportation Center(TTC). Once you are at the TTC, you can catch a bus to Hollywood Studios. The only Disney transportation available between Old Key West and Disney's Hollywood Studios is a bus. Boats run from Hollywood Studios to the Epcot area resorts (Swan and Dolphin, Yacht & Beach Clubs, Boardwalk) and to Epcot.
Thank you for stopping by the Disney Parks Moms Panel. I hope you have a magical vacation with smooth transportation!
Amy H.

Mount Batur Sunrise Trekking
About This Activity:
- All Inclusive
- Private Tour
- Pick Up & Drop
- 6 - 8 Hours
- Live Tour Guide English
- Watch the spectacular sunrise from Mount Batur summit.
- Enjoy panoramic views of Lake Batur and surrounding mountains.
- Have breakfast while enjoying the morning scenery.
- Trek with an experienced local guide.
- Visit a traditional Balinese coffee plantation.
Join our Mount Batur Sunrise Trekking tour and discover why it is one of the most unforgettable experiences in Bali. Trek through the early morning darkness with a professional local guide and reach the summit just in time to watch the sunrise illuminate the volcanic landscape.
From the top, enjoy stunning views of Lake Batur, surrounding mountains, and the beautiful Bali countryside. After breakfast at the summit, continue your journey with a visit to a traditional Balinese coffee plantation before returning comfortably to your hotel. Perfect for adventure seekers, nature lovers, and anyone wanting to experience Bali from a unique perspective.
About Mount Batur
Mount Batur is an active volcano located in Kintamani, Bali, standing at 1,717 meters above sea level. Famous for its spectacular sunrise views, Mount Batur attracts thousands of visitors every year who come to experience one of the best trekking adventures in Bali. The trek is suitable for beginners with a reasonable level of fitness and offers breathtaking views of Lake Batur, Mount Abang, and the surrounding volcanic landscape.
Prices:
- 2-10 Person IDR 650.000/person
- 10 + Person IDR 600.000/person
- Meet up at Parking= IDR 375.000 /person (Minimum 2 person)
- For 1 Person or Solo Traveler IDR 1.300.000 /person
Ready for the Best Sunrise Experience in Bali?
Book your Mount Batur Sunrise Trekking today and enjoy an unforgettable combination of volcano trekking, stunning sunrise views
Contact us via WhatsApp for instant confirmation and availability.
- Hotel pick up drive directly to starting point
- 03.30 am, arrival at starting point,
- 03.45 am, Begin trail trek up to sunrise point/peak accompanied by the licensed professional trekking guides
- 05. 45 am, Arrival at the sunrise point where we enjoy the spectacular sunrise view and enjoy the beakfast
- 06.30-07.00 am, after the sunrise, we continue the trek to see the friendly monkeys around the main crater
- 07.30 am, begin descent. While descent you will enjoy the view
- 08.30 am, Trek is finished, you will drive back to the hotel
- 09.00 am, Stop off at a Balinese coffee plantation.
- 10.00 am- 11.45 am, Arrival at the hotel (Depend on which hotel you are staying).
Inclusions & Excludes
- Pick up and return to your hotel by private air conditioned car
- Comfortable air conditioning car with english speaking driver
- Experienced private trekking guides English speaking
- Entrance Fee to Kintamani Area
- Visiting coffee plantation during on the way back to the hotel. (An extra trip after hike, you can skip or visit)
- Trekking equipment such as, Torch (flashlight)
- Hot tea or Coffe
- Mineral Water
- All Your Personal Expenses
What to Bring
- Hiking shoes or sport shoes.
- Warm jacket & Long pants.
- Backpack & camera
Details Pick up Time
- Ubud : 02.30 AM
- Sanur : 02.00 AM
- Kuta,Legian,Seminyak : 01.00 – 01.40 AM
- Activity Level : Moderate
- Hiking Duration : 4 Hours (up & down)
- Temperature :8 – 15° Celsius (At the summit)
- Women are not allowed to climb up the Volcano during their menstruation period
- Bring only what you need, the rest leave them in your hotel
- Some cash for tipping the guide and driver is recommended
Frequently Asked Questions
Is Mount Batur trekking suitable for beginners?
Yes. The trek is considered moderate and suitable for most people with basic fitness.
What should I bring?
Comfortable shoes, a jacket, camera, and personal essentials.
What time is hotel pickup?
Usually between 2:00 AM and 3:00 AM depending on your location.
Is breakfast included?
Yes, breakfast is served at the summit.
Can children join the trek?
Yes, children can join with parental supervision.
