CORNMAZE + PUMPKIN PATCH
During the month of October we are open to the public on Saturdays and Sundays. The October festival is a self-guided tour of our farm that features the two-acre cornmaze, hayrides, visiting and feeding the animals, and plenty of barnyard play areas for children. We also have pumpkins for sale. We are family friendly and welcome you out to our farm to enjoy the fall fun together!
- Saturday, October 3rd (10am-6pm)
- Sunday, October 4th (1pm-6pm)
- Friday, October 9th (10am-4pm)
- Saturday, October 10th (10am-6pm)
- Sunday, October 11th (1pm-6pm)
- Saturday, October 17th (10am-6pm)
- Sunday, October 18th (1pm-6pm)
- Saturday, October 24th (10am-6pm)
- Sunday, October 25th (1pm-6pm)
Admission is $12 per person for everyone ages 2 and up. All activities are included in this admission cost.
Cornmaze, Hayrides, Petting + Feeding the Animals, Barnyard Games for the kids, and Free Popcorn.
***Open weekends in October only
Carving sized pumpkins are available for purchase.
FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS
Do you require reservations?
We do not take reservations. Our limiting factor is parking, which is available on a first come first come basis.
Do you take cash or card?
We accept both forms of payments. There is a 3% surcharge added to all credit card transactions to cover usage fees.
Are you pet friendly?
We ask that you leave your furry friends at home. Visiting our farm allows you to come into close contact with our farm animals, which many dogs are not familiar with. So to ensure the best experience for our animals, your pets, and our other guests at the farm... we ask that you leave your pets at home.
Do you grow your own pumpkins?
We have some pumpkins grown on our farm and others are brought in from a farm in the mountains.
What animals do you have?
We have cows, a donkey, chickens, and goats.
Do you serve food?
We offer free popcorn with admission and sell sodas, bottled water, hot fresh mini donuts, and fresh local milk.
How large is the maze and how long does it take?
Our maze is right around 2 acres. It typically takes folks between 20-30 minutes to complete. We do have a map available for those who don't care to be lost.
Do we have to pay admission to just buy pumpkins?
If you are interested in just purchasing pumpkins and not participating in any activities (feeding animals, hayrides, cornmaze, etc.) you do not have to pay the admission fee.
Does weather affect open hours?
Because 100% of our activities are outdoors, we will close down for inclement weather if needed. Please check social media for updates regarding changes in hours due to weather.

