Interesting facts about the Evektor SportStar SLM
✈ The Evektor SportStar SLM is a lightweight, two-seat sport aircraft developed and manufactured by Evektor-Aerotechnik in Kunovice, Czech Republic.
✈ It is part of the successful SportStar family and was designed to meet the growing demand for modern, affordable light sport flying.
✈ The aircraft seats two people in a side-by-side configuration, making it ideal for sport flying, pilot training, and leisure touring.
✈ The SportStar SLM is powered by the Rotax 912ULS engine, delivering 100 horsepower with exceptional fuel efficiency.
✈ Its metal airframe construction ensures durability and low maintenance costs, which appeals to both private owners and flying clubs.
✈ The aircraft offers a wide range of avionics options, including glass cockpit systems for enhanced training and modern flying experiences.
✈ The SportStar SLM is valued for its low operating costs, making it a cost-effective alternative to traditional GA trainers such as the Cessna 150 and 152.
✈ Evektor exports the SportStar SLM globally, with customers in Europe, North America, Asia, and Australia using it for recreational and training roles.
