If your business handles complex projects and requires a more structured approach, I can help you establish or improve your Project Management Office (PMO). Whether you’re looking to better manage resources, streamline project timelines, or enhance budget controls, a well-designed PMO is essential to long-term success.
I’ll help you implement the systems and frameworks needed to manage multiple projects efficiently. From initial setup to continuous improvement, I work with your team to ensure your PMO delivers tangible results.
A strong PMO is more than just a framework for managing projects—it’s a strategic asset that drives efficiency and project success. I work with businesses to create PMOs that are tailored, scalable, and effective.
I help establish a PMO framework that fits your business, whether you’re just starting out or looking to enhance an existing setup. I focus on governance, resource allocation, and project delivery, ensuring that your PMO supports your goals and scales as your business grows.
Using tools like ProjectWorks, I ensure that the system is implemented efficiently, enabling your business to manage complex project scheduling, resource allocation, and budget tracking with ease. This includes full configuration of the tool to suit your business's unique requirements.
If you need help establishing a PMO or improving your current framework, I offer project-based support to get your PMO up and running quickly.
For continuous support and improvement, I provide ongoing PMO management, ensuring that your project management processes stay effective and aligned with your evolving business needs.
Build a Project Management Office (PMO) that empowers your business to handle complex projects, optimize resources, and control budgets efficiently. From initial setup to ongoing improvement, I help you create a scalable PMO framework that aligns with your unique goals and drives real results.
Gisch Consulting offers a fully guided and supported process for selecting, testing and implementing a project management solution to help SMEs embrace cloud productivity solutions.

HOUSE LOGO . BRANDING
Client:
Tim McMullan, a transformational coach and intuitive consultant, returned to awen&co for a personal project: a custom logo for the East Hampton home he and his husband built. The modern house, with striking gabled forms clad in shou sugi ban, has been featured in architecture publications and earned top design awards.
Challenge:
Tim wanted a handcrafted, sophisticated logo that reflected the home’s elegance and could work on everything from cocktail napkins to apparel. It needed to feel personal, modern, and timeless.
Our Role:
We were commissioned to create two logo versions celebrating the home: one a simple black filled line drawing, and the other incorporating a hand-drawn shou sugi ban texture within the same footprint. Both needed to feel timeless, versatile, and reflective of the home’s architectural character.
Approach:
We drew inspiration from the home’s gabled forms and shou sugi ban cladding, studying its architectural lines to guide the logo’s structure. The two concepts allowed for flexibility, one minimal and modern, the other textured and detailed, both capturing the home’s sophistication in a personal, handcrafted way.
Creative Direction:
The final logos combine clean, modern geometry with artisanal touches, subtly referencing the shou sugi ban texture of the home. This approach ensures the designs work beautifully across formats, from small gifts to apparel, celebrating the house’s architectural elegance.
outcome:
Tim and his husband loved the final logos, which now serve as a meaningful, versatile symbol of their home. The designs complement a house that has earned accolades such as Best Weekend Home in the 2024 Interior Design NYCxDESIGN Awards and Exterior Architecture in the 2024 Luxe RED Awards, translating its architectural distinction into a personal, refined identity.
"They went above and beyond in designing our brand identity"
The entire design team at Awen & Co were fantastic to work with. They took time to learn about us and our company and did a lot of research behind the scenes to understand our industry and particular needs. They went above and beyond in designing our brand identity including our logo, brandmark, supporting graphics and an awesome pattern. They even came out to our space to paint a mural for us. Even more than that, we feel like we have gained some new friends! Highly recommend!
— Deanna Varney, co-founder of Wavelength Coffee Roasters

