I got BabyEbi a small squirty bottle today, he still has trouble shooting in the right direction but it will come with practice. I use soda water - yes, the stuff you usually mix with your drinks, to clean windows and glass. NOTHING makes them sparkle so well, the first time you try it you might have to do it a couple of times to get rid of the chemical build up from previous cleaners, but once that is gone you will be amazed. Just squirt and rub dry with a soft cloth, towelling is good. PLUS it is totally safe to let little ones loose with it, good for the environment too.

Regula lui 40%
vineri, iunie 26th, 2015
A few months ago, I blogged about a formula I came across at a board meeting a while back that says your year over year growth rate plus your pre-tax operating margins need to be at least forty percent. Meaning you can grow at 100% per year and have operating margins of -60%. Or you can have flat growth and have 40% operating margins. Or you can grow at 20% per year and have 20% operating margins. There is no magic to the forty percent target, but I do like establishing some relationship between acceptable levels of profitability (or losses) and growth. Too many times I have seen companies invest in growth for growth sake without having any constraints or sanity checks on that investment and the losses that result from that investment.
This entry was posted on vineri, iunie 26th, 2015 at 07:46 and is filed under business, Internet. You can follow any responses to this entry through the RSS 2.0 feed. You can leave a response, or trackback from your own site.

However, the proportions of your hot tub might influence your enjoyment and ownership experience.
A hot tub in your garden may be a fantasy come true. The purpose of your 20-minute dip in a hot tub is to enjoy the experience. (All right, let’s be honest: it’s probably closer to an hour.) You’re loving the sensation of the jets on your back and the way your body relaxes in the warm temperature. You’re not considering life’s big concerns since your head is resting on a soft spa cushion.
You may go outside at any moment to unwind in the comfort of your own little paradise. But how can you go from wanting to acquire a hot tub to actually purchasing one? You plan in the same way that you would create any vision into reality. You are most likely not thinking about the proportions of the hot tub while you rest.
While there are several things to consider when selecting the ideal home spa model, such as the power of its jets, the effectiveness of its heater, and the maintenance necessary for its filtration system, the most crucial is also the most basic: size.
So, take your ruler and continue reading!
Spas are available in a range of sizes to accommodate a variety of settings and backyards. When looking for the greatest spa, it’s crucial to consider hot tub proportions as well as the exciting features like jets and LED lights.
Standard hot tub sizes are 78×78″, 84×84″, and 94×94″. Depending on the model, the depth (or height) of the spa might vary.
How do you select a hot tub with the proper dimensions? There are various considerations that will influence your selection.
Table of Contents
The Importance of Knowing Your Space
Having a personal hot tub in their backyard is a dream come true for many homeowners. However, if you’ve decided to buy a hot tub, one of the first stages toward ownership is selecting where you’ll install your new whirlpool. Once you’ve determined the best location for your new hot tub, it’s critical to become acquainted with common hot tub measurements so that you can pick the proper turbo spa and assure a great fit! Keeping in mind the restrictions of your area as well as how you intend to use the tub, such as whether you intend to bathe alone or with others, can help you have a pleasant experience with your new tub.
One of the most common spa sizes is 94×94″, which is around 8×8′. It is critical to examine the depth or height. Soaking might be more pleasant with the extra depth. Furthermore, the height can influence how easy it moves into the area.
How Big is a Hot Tub?
Before you buy a hot tub, you need know how large it is. The usual size of a hot tub is between 7 and 8 feet square. However, there are some that are as large as 9 feet broad and 9 feet long. There are spas that accommodate two to three people and take up little room.
You will require a place that is greater than the size of the hot tub. Why? Access to the service panel, clearance for a cover lifter (if used), and a place for the steps must all be considered.
Furthermore, while laying the concrete pad, builders often recommend adding one foot to the spa measurements — at the very least. The extra foot will provide you with six inches of space on either side.
It is also critical to have easy access to the area of your prospective hot tub. If you have a fence, the gate should be broader than the spa’s height. Hot tubs are frequently transported on their side, whether by forklift or dolly. They can be transported by crane in certain conditions.
The TS 240, for example, is a 78×78″ two-person hot tub. This hot tub may be built both indoors and outside.
Hot Tub Dimensions Comparison
Many hot tubs are classified into three sizes: small spas for two to three people, medium spas for four to six people, and giant spas for seven or more people.
Tiny hot tub dimensions: Master Spas manufactures two small hot tubs. The Getaway San Miguel is 69×79′′ in size. The dimensions of the TS 240, a corner hot tub, are 78×78′′.
Dimensions of the large spa: Perhaps you have a large family or like entertaining. Alternatively, you may like a hot tub large enough to include a float and relax in throughout the summer. (Yes, it’s a thing, and you should try it if you haven’t already!) A hot tub with measurements such as 94″ by 94″ might help you meet your requirements.
Are you looking for a larger spa? The Clarity Spas Balance 9 and Michael Phelps Legend Series LSX 900, both with dimensions of 108′′ x 94′′, are among the largest Master Spas models.
If your hot tub will be in a tight place, the height of the spa may need to be considered.
The Most Important Factor?
Many individuals base their assessment of the size of a hot tub on the number of seats. However, there is another critical characteristic to consider: height.
Why should you take height into account while determining spa dimensions?
First, as previously said, the height might influence how the spa is provided. A shallower model may fit through a tighter opening. If you wish to place your hot tub indoors or on a screened-in porch, it must fit through the doorway. The spa will be supplied based on its dimensions; thus the height is the most important factor to consider.
Some spa manufacturers, such as the Twilight Series TS 67.25, produce 34-inch-tall spas. The dimensions of this little hot tub are 70′′ x 84′′ x 34′′. OK. It’s time to pause and rewind. Keep in mind the warm water, the jets, and the cushion beneath your head.
When it comes to soaking, a hot tub with more depth and area in the foot well may be more pleasant. As the depth of the water increases, the buoyancy of the water changes, easing even more tension and strain on the joints. Plus, if you are taller, you will have more room to stretch out and relax
Standard Hot Tub Dimensions
Typically, spa manufacturers offer three size categories to choose from:
- Small Hot Tubs: 2-4 people
- Medium Hot Tubs: 5-6 people
- Large Hot Tubs: 7+ people.
Unfortunately, there is no such thing as a conventional size for a hot tub. A four-person hot tub, for example, may only comfortably accommodate two or three individuals, depending on their size, shape, and demand for personal space. Not only that, but the seating layout, water depth, and width and breadth of the tub can all vary dramatically from one brand of hot tub to the next.
On the one hand, this is fantastic; no matter what your preferences are, you’ll be able to locate a hot tub that suits you. On the other side, it makes comparing or simply narrowing down the possibilities difficult.
Within these sizing categories, there are different length, width, and height options, so it’s important to check with your hot tub dealer to determine the exact dimensions of the model you want. Standard hot tub dimensions are as follows:
- Small Hot Tubs: 5’4” – 7” (Length) x 5’4” – 6’8” (Width) x 29” – 35” (Height)
- Medium Hot Tubs: 6’6” – 7’9” (Length) x 6’4” – 7’9” (Width) x 33” – 38.5” (Height)
- Large: 7’ – 9” (Length) x 7’ – 9’2” (Width) x 36” – 38” (Height)
Choosing a Hot Tub Based on Size
Hot tub collections from spa manufacturers contain a variety of models with distinctive style and feature combinations.
While it is critical to compare hot tub models within each series, the size within a series has an influence on pricing.
With this in mind, start your search for a new hot tub by evaluating your budget and the amount of people who will be using the spa at the same time. Consider a 7-person hot tub if you have a large family or want to invite friends and neighbours over for a dip from time to time.
If not, a smaller choice, such as a 3-person hot tub, may be preferable. Remember that individuals, like hot tubs, come in a variety of sizes. Depending on who is in it, the 6-person hot tub may feel roomier.
Once you’ve decided on the perfect hot tub model, consider entertainment options for your spa and the accessories you desire. After that, it’s time to think about spa location, delivery, and installation.
Hot Tub Dimensions Influence Location, Delivery, and Installation
A necessary part of making your home spa dream a reality is choosing the best placement for your hot tub, how you’re going to get it there, and how to properly install it.
Location.
You’ll need to choose a spot that’s large enough for your hot tub and its foundation. You’ll also want to make sure the space will accommodate your spa cover lifter (each cover lifter requires a small amount of additional clearance). The best way to know you’ve chosen the best spot is to ask your local dealer, who will be handling delivery.
Delivery.
You won’t have to worry about delivery concerns if your hot tub site has easy access. However, if the road from the street to your spa is constrained, you will need to clear enough space. This might entail pruning tree branches or removing pieces of a fence or gate. When ground delivery is not possible, several dealers offer cranes to raise your new hot tub into place. So, before scheduling delivery, walk the route, measure clearance around the walkway, and compare your measurements to the dimensions of the spa.
Hot tub measurements are important not only when evaluating your area, but also when considering the practicalities of the actual delivery of your hot tub. It is critical to inspect your area and examine its accessibility for delivery in order to ensure a smooth, trouble-free delivery.
The delivery will be easier if the way from the street to your spa is clear. If the path is more constrained, it is critical to clear adequate space or ask your dealer if they have the necessary equipment to hoist your new hot tub into place if ground delivery is not possible.
Fortunately, your hot tub will be delivered “dry,” allowing it to be flipped on its side for transportation. Because of this, horizontal clearance is crucial, therefore measure the height of your hot tub. If the delivery path contains sharp, tight bends or overhead barriers, such as low-hanging trees or a lintel over a fence gate, the length and breadth of your spa are critical. Each hot tub model comes with its own pre-delivery instructions, which contain hot tub specifications as well as preparation and installation information, to assist make the delivery process go as smoothly as possible.
Installation.
How you prepare for installation will be determined on the size of your hot tub. All spas need a solid base. A large, hefty spa needs a concrete slab base at least 4″ thick. A concrete slab is required for most spas, including the 8-person ones. If you intend to place the spa on a deck, ensure sure it can withstand 610 kg/m2. Level your site and prepare your foundation ahead of time, because most delivery staff will not do this for you and will be unable to install your hot tub until this is completed.
Whether you want a little or big home spa, or anything in the between, there are plenty of size, feature, and accessory options to select from. Then all you have to do is relax and enjoy your new hot tub.
Hot Tub Weight
The weight of the hot tub is also a significant factor in its size. An empty hot tub typically weights 225 to 450 kgs. Your foundation should be able to resist not just the weight of the tub, but also the water and the people, to guarantee proper structural support.
A modest hot tub full with water and passengers will weigh around 1350 kilos. A medium-sized hot tub in the same condition will weigh around 2000 kg, while a big hot tub will weigh around 2,500 kg.
Hot Tub Pad Size
Hot tubs can be placed on wooden decking if there is adequate support, but many homeowners choose to pour a concrete pad instead. The pad should be, at minimum, the same size as the hot tub.

The Brazilian farmer survey serves as a both a forecast of crop size and analysis of the state of the crop, compiled from trusted sources such as farmers and agronomists. Its goal is not only to forecast the Brazilian crop but also to break down the forecast by regions and varieties, while highlighting the factors influencing the results. 
Survey conducted Jul 10-11, 2025.
It provides a comprehensive understanding of the Brazilian crop, covering factors such as age, farmer investment, weather conditions, crop size, and regional variability. With each survey, we gather more data, allowing us to refine our analysis over the years, building a valuable backlog of Brazil data from past surveys.
