Grilled Mushrooms for Steak
Garlicky grilled mushrooms make a tasty topping for a steak or burgers.
What is this button?
You now are able to shop & buy these ingredients online! After you select your market, you decide if you want to have your items delivered or picked up today!
8 ounces fresh baby bella mushrooms, washed, stems removed, quartered
1 Half Stick (1/4 cup) Land O Lakes® Butter
12 teaspoon finely chopped fresh garlic
1 teaspoon dried parsley flakes
18 teaspoon salt
How to make
- STEP 1 Heat gas grill to medium-high or charcoal grill until coals are ash white.
- STEP 2 Place mushrooms into center of 18-inch square sheet of heavy-duty aluminum foil.
- STEP 3 Cut butter into small pieces. Place over mushrooms. Sprinkle mushrooms with garlic, parsley and salt. Bring long sides of foil up over mushrooms; seal using double folds. Seal remaining sides of foil using double folds.
- STEP 4 Place packet directly onto grill. Close cover; grill 15-20 minutes or until mushrooms are cooked through and tender.
- STEP 5 Carefully open packet with scissors, allowing steam to escape. Stir mushrooms; spoon over steak or potatoes.
When cooking on a grill, use heavy-duty aluminum foil.
This recipe can be made on the stovetop. Heat butter over medium-high heat in 10-inch skillet until bubbles form. Add mushrooms, garlic, parsley and salt; cook stirring occasionally, 3-5 minutes or until mushrooms are tender and glazed.
And don't forget to tag us @landolakesktchn.
