- Bad outlets: Outlets that don’t work or feel warm to touch can be a fire risk.
- Burning smells: Any smell of burning from outlets or wires is a serious warning sign.
- Overloaded circuits: If you use too many devices on one circuit, it can cause problems.
- Sparking outlets: Sparks from outlets are never normal and need quick fixing.
- Strange noises: Buzzing or humming from outlets or switches can mean trouble.
- Hot switch plates: If your switch plates feel hot, there might be a wiring issue.
- Dimming lights: Lights that dim when you use other appliances may show an overloaded system.
