dnssec-dsfromkey — DNSSEC DS RR generation tool
dnssec-dsfromkey  [-v ] [level-1] [-2] [-a ] [alg-C] [-l ] [domain-T ] {keyfile}TTL
dnssec-dsfromkey  {-s} [-1] [-2] [-a ] [alg-K ] [directory-l ] [domain-s] [-c ] [class-T ] [TTL-f ] [file-A] [-v ] {dnsname}level
dnssec-dsfromkey  [-h] [-V]
dnssec-dsfromkey outputs the Delegation Signer (DS) resource record (RR), as defined in RFC 3658 and RFC 4509, for the given key(s).
Use SHA-1 as the digest algorithm (the default is to use both SHA-1 and SHA-256).
Use SHA-256 as the digest algorithm.
            Select the digest algorithm. The value of
            algorithm must be one of SHA-1 (SHA1),
            SHA-256 (SHA256), GOST or SHA-384 (SHA384).
            These values are case insensitive.
          
Generate CDS records rather than DS records. This is mutually exclusive with generating lookaside records.
Specifies the TTL of the DS records.
            Look for key files (or, in keyset mode,
            keyset- files) in
            directory.
          
            Zone file mode: in place of the keyfile name, the argument is
            the DNS domain name of a zone master file, which can be read
            from file.  If the zone name is the same as
            file, then it may be omitted.
          
            If file is set to "-", then
            the zone data is read from the standard input.  This makes it
            possible to use the output of the dig
            command as input, as in:
          
            dig dnskey example.com | dnssec-dsfromkey -f - example.com
          
Include ZSK's when generating DS records. Without this option, only keys which have the KSK flag set will be converted to DS records and printed. Useful only in zone file mode.
            Generate a DLV set instead of a DS set.  The specified
            domain is appended to the name for each
            record in the set.
            The DNSSEC Lookaside Validation (DLV) RR is described
            in RFC 4431.  This is mutually exclusive with generating
	    CDS records.
          
Keyset mode: in place of the keyfile name, the argument is the DNS domain name of a keyset file.
Specifies the DNS class (default is IN). Useful only in keyset or zone file mode.
Sets the debugging level.
Prints usage information.
Prints version information.
      To build the SHA-256 DS RR from the
      keyfile name, the following command would be issued:
    
dnssec-dsfromkey -2 Kexample.com.+003+26160
    
The command would print something like:
example.com. IN DS 26160 5 2 3A1EADA7A74B8D0BA86726B0C227AA85AB8BBD2B2004F41A868A54F0 C5EA0B94
    
BIND 9.9.9b2 (Extended Support Version)

When it comes to efficient supply chain management, iWare Supplychain Services Ltd. is setting new industry standards. With the unveiling of their latest iWare Supplychain Warehousing Facility in Nagpur, they’re not just expanding their footprint—they’re revolutionizing how logistics are done for Shakti Pumps Ltd. This move is a game-changer, aimed at optimizing the supply chain processes for Shakti Pumps, a brand known for its energy-efficient water pumping solutions.
This strategic initiative is more than just about storage space; it’s about supply chain efficiency, cost optimization, and delivering superior customer experiences. Positioned in Nagpur, a crucial logistics hub in India, this new Shakti Pumps Warehousing Facility is poised to transform how Shakti Pumps manages its inventory and distribution.
But why is this so important? And what makes this facility stand out from other warehousing units? Let’s dive in to see how this development is set to reshape the industry landscape.
Why Nagpur is the Perfect Choice for Shakti Pumps Warehousing
Choosing Nagpur as the location for the new Shakti Pumps Warehousing Facility wasn’t just a random decision. Nagpur holds a strategic advantage due to its central location in India. It serves as a critical junction connecting major cities, ensuring faster distribution and reducing transit times significantly.
The facility is strategically situated at Khasra No. 201/1, Mouza Waddhamna Village, Tehsil Hingna, Nagpur, which offers excellent connectivity to national highways and railway networks. This means Shakti Pumps can now efficiently cater to demand from multiple regions, enhancing their market reach and minimizing logistical costs.
But location isn’t the only factor that sets this iWare Supplychain Warehousing Facility apart. It’s about the infrastructure, technology, and strategic foresight that have gone into its development. This facility is designed to maximize storage efficiency, streamline operations, and ensure timely delivery of Shakti Pumps’ products, reinforcing their reputation for reliability and customer satisfaction.
Inside the iWare Supplychain Warehousing Facility
This isn’t your average storage space. The new iWare Supplychain Warehousing Facility is built with cutting-edge technology to support the growing demands of Shakti Pumps. From advanced inventory management systems to automated material handling, every aspect of this facility is designed for efficiency.
One of the standout features is its space optimization strategy. The facility is meticulously planned to utilize every square foot effectively, ensuring maximum storage without compromising on accessibility. This makes inventory management smoother and faster, reducing lead times and enhancing operational efficiency.
Moreover, the facility is equipped with real-time tracking systems that provide live updates on inventory levels. This ensures accurate order fulfillment and minimizes the risk of stockouts or overstocking. With such robust systems in place, Shakti Pumps Warehousing operations are set to become more efficient than ever before.
Security and Safety First
Security is a top priority for iWare. The facility features 24/7 surveillance systems, advanced access control, and fire safety measures, ensuring that Shakti Pumps’ inventory is safeguarded at all times. This isn’t just about protecting products—it’s about building trust and reliability.
The Strategic Partnership Between iWare and Shakti Pumps
This collaboration isn’t just about logistics; it’s about strategic growth. Shakti Pumps has long been a market leader in energy-efficient water pumping solutions. However, tomaintain their competitive edge, they needed a logistics partner who could keep pace with their innovation and growth. Enter iWare Supplychain Services Ltd.
Why Shakti Pumps Chose iWare
Shakti Pumps selected iWare because of their comprehensive logistics solutions and their reputation for operational excellence. As part of the Inter India Group, iWare boasts a vast operational network with over 804,466 square feet across 11 warehouses in seven states, including Gujarat, West Bengal, Uttar Pradesh, Rajasthan, Punjab, Haryana, and Delhi.
This partnership allows Shakti Pumps to leverage iWare’s Third-Party Logistics (3PL) expertise, ensuring seamless inventory management and efficient distribution. By outsourcing logistics to iWare, Shakti Pumps can now focus on their core strength—developing innovative energy-efficient pumping solutions.
Mutual Benefits and Strategic Goals
For Shakti Pumps, the new Shakti Pumps Warehousing Facility translates to reduced lead times, improved customer satisfaction, and cost-effective supply chain operations. For iWare, this collaboration solidifies their position as a leader in the logistics industry, expanding their footprint and showcasing their capabilities in advanced warehousing solutions.
Together, they’re not just optimizing logistics—they’re setting new standards for supply chain efficiency and customer satisfaction.
How This iWare Supplychain Warehousing Facility Benefits Shakti Pumps
The benefits of this state-of-the-art iWare Supplychain Warehousing Facility are multifaceted. Here’s how it impacts Shakti Pumps’ operations:
- Enhanced Inventory Management: Advanced systems allow real-time tracking of inventory, reducing the chances of stockouts and overstocking.
- Faster Distribution: The strategic location in Nagpur ensures quicker delivery to multiple regions, enhancing customer satisfaction.
- Cost Optimization: Efficient logistics operations reduce transportation and operational costs, boosting profitability.
- Operational Efficiency: Automated handling and streamlined processes increase productivity, ensuring timely order fulfillment.
- Scalability and Growth: The facility is designed to support Shakti Pumps’ growth trajectory, ensuring they can meet rising market demand.
By utilizing the Shakti Pumps Warehousing Facility, Shakti Pumps is not just improving their logistics—they’re redefining supply chain efficiency.
Impact on the Local Economy and Industry
The new iWare Supplychain Warehousing Facility isn’t just good news for Shakti Pumps—it’s also a boon for the local economy. By setting up this advanced facility in Nagpur, iWare is creating employment opportunities and supporting local businesses. From staffing and security to local suppliers and logistics partners, the economic impact is widespread.
Moreover, this facility strengthens Nagpur’s position as a logistics hub, attracting more investments and fostering regional economic growth. It’s not just about warehousing; it’s about community development and economic empowerment.
- What makes this Shakti Pumps Warehousing Facility special?
It’s strategically located in Nagpur, equipped with advanced inventory systems, and designed for maximum operational efficiency.
- Why did Shakti Pumps choose iWare for warehousing?
iWare offers comprehensive 3PL solutions, advanced logistics technology, and an extensive operational network.
- How does this facility impact Shakti Pumps’ supply chain?
It reduces lead times, enhances inventory management, and optimizes logistics costs, ensuring timely deliveries.
Why is Nagpur a strategic choice for this facility?
Nagpur’s central location offers superior connectivity, reducing transit times and logistics costs across India.
Conclusion: A New Era for Shakti Pumps and iWare
The launch of the iWare Supplychain Warehousing Facility in Nagpur marks a strategic milestone for both iWare and Shakti Pumps. By combining state-of-the-art technology, strategic location, and unmatched logistics expertise, they’re setting new standards in supply chain efficiency.This partnership is about more than just logistics; it’s about strategic growth, customer satisfaction, and industry leadership. As iWare continues to expand and innovate, they’re not just keeping up with industry trends—they’re leading them.

