San Diego Strikeforce vs Bay Area Panthers IFL at Frontwave Arena
The Indoor Football League (IFL) is the longest continuously-running indoor football league in the United States and the second-longest-running professional football league in the country, behind only the NFL.With 14 teams spanning across the country, the IFL is the largest and most prominent indoor football league in the nation, boasting the only true national footprint in the sport. The league operates in 8 of the top 50 media markets, with continued expansion expected in the coming years.
The IFL delivers an electrifying brand of football, played on a 50-yard field surrounded by padded dasher boards. Each team plays with 8 players on offense and defense, with two offensive players allowed in motion at the snap, creating an explosive, high-scoring game that keeps fans on the edge of their seats. Teams compete in a 16-game regular season, leading up to the IFL Playoffs and the IFL National Championship.
