Apps are ready-made tools for the jobs teams do most - transcripts, spreadsheets, documents, images, video, music and speech - each with a focused screen of its own.
Chat can do almost anything, but some jobs deserve a purpose-built screen: a drop zone for recordings, a row-by-row runner for spreadsheets, a player for generated audio. Apps are those screens. Open Apps in the left sidebar to see them all. Each one picks sensible defaults, shows the settings that matter for that job, and keeps a history of what you made.
| App | What it does | Guide | 
| Transcript | Convert audio to text by speakers. | Transcription | 
| Excel AI | Process an Excel file row by row. | Excel AI | 
| Document Editor | Create or modify a document with a prompt, then refine it by versioned edits. | Document editor | 
| Image Generation | Create a new image from text. | Images and image editing | 
| Image Manipulation | Drop an image and describe how you want to transform or extend it. | Images and image editing | 
| Video Generation | Create a video from a text prompt. | Video generation | 
| Music Generation | Create music from a text prompt. | Music and text to speech | 
| Text to Speech | Turn text into natural-sounding spoken audio. | Music and text to speech | 
| Compare Models | Test multiple AI models side by side. | Compare models | 
The small print on each card names the formats or model families involved, such as XLSX · XLS · CSV for Excel AI or VEO · SORA · SEEDANCE for video.
Where apps show up
- Apps page. The full list, from Apps in the sidebar.
- Home. The home page’s What would you like to do? row offers the most common apps right under the composer.
- Results stay put. Transcripts and documents keep their own lists, and generated videos, tracks and speech each get a result page with a Download button.
Apps use credits like chats do. Result pages for transcripts, videos, music and speech show what each one cost. Media generation - especially video - uses noticeably more credits than a text answer, so it pays to get the prompt right before you generate. Your workspace’s consumption is on the sidebar usage meter; admins see the detail in Usage and billing.

