Wollongong, located in the Illawarra region of New South Wales, is a coastal city known for its stunning natural landscapes and outdoor activities. Situated along the Grand Pacific Drive, it offers surfing beaches, rock pools, and scenic trails around Mt. Keira in the Illawarra mountain range. To the north, visitors can watch hang gliders launch from Bald Hill while to the south lies Lake Illawarra and the Nan Tien Buddhist temple.1% as popular as Sydney29 minutes off the main route, 55% of way to Bowral
Sights & LandmarksGovernment BuildingsPoints of Interest & LandmarksThe Municipality of Kiama is a picturesque local government area in New South Wales, Australia, located south of Shellharbour and the City of Wollongong. Nestled beside the Pacific Ocean, it offers stunning coastal views and easy access via the Princes Highway and South Coast railway line. Visitors can enjoy diverse dining experiences such as JJ's Indian Restaurant, known for its vegetarian-friendly options and consistently good reviews on various platforms.1% as popular as Sydney41 minutes off the main route, 60% of way to Bowral
The top stops along the way from Mosman to Bowral (with short detours) are Sydney Opera House, Port Jackson Bay, and Circular Quay Wharf 3. Other popular stops include Bondi to Coogee Walk, Sydney Harbour Bridge, and Palm Beach.
