Highly recommended 👍🏼👍🏼👍🏼👍🏼Mi F — Google reviewLoved the zoo, especially the chimps and gorillas. Great location for the amazing bird show with full view of the Sydney harbour. Sea lion show is very popular, make sure to join the queue ahead of time for a seat in shade. Public transport options are very good, both the bus and ferry. Tiger, lions and a few other animals were sleeping on a hot day. The themed sections are easy to navigate with a map.A D — Google reviewTaronga Zoo is a fantastic experience and one of the best attractions in Sydney. The zoo is beautifully laid out, making it easy to walk through and enjoy clear views of many different animal species. The Australian natives are especially impressive — the koalas are a major highlight, and seeing the duck‑billed platypus, kangaroos, and other unique wildlife up close was unforgettable.
The staff and volunteers were incredibly friendly, helpful, and clearly passionate about the animals. Their warmth really added to the visit.
It rained for most of the day, which dampened the experience a little, but even with the weather, we still had a wonderful time. On a sunny day, it would have been even better. Highly recommended for anyone visiting Sydney.David K — Google reviewDuring my recent trip to Australia, I got a wonderful opportunity to visit the Taronga Zoo—and it turned out to be one of the most memorable experiences of the trip. I chose to go on the last day, which meant limited time, but the journey itself made it special. I walked from my hotel to Circular Quay, took a ferry, and honestly—that ferry ride deserves a story of its own (will share that experience later!). From the ferry point, I took a bus directly to the zoo entrance. I reached a little early, so I waited outside while the ticket counters opened at 9:00 AM (zoo entry starts at 9:30 AM). The ticket cost 55 AUD. I spent some buffer time exploring the zoo shop and grabbing a quick bite at the restaurant.
Once inside, the real experience began. The zoo had different sections—Australia, Africa, and Asia (if I remember correctly). I started with the Australian section, and it was absolutely magical. I saw beautiful and rare birds, lemurs, kangaroos, koalas, dingoes, emus, mulgaras, platypus, and many more incredible species.
Everything was well-organized, clean, and beautifully maintained. The environment, the layout, and the natural design made the entire experience feel immersive and calming.
Even with limited time, it was full of fun, discovery, and joy—a truly memorable experience and one that I’ll always cherish from my Australia trip 🇦🇺✨Swaraj ( — Google reviewWe had a wonderful visit to Taronga Zoo with our kids — it’s truly one of the best family-friendly attractions in Sydney! From the moment we arrived, we were impressed by how clean, well-organised and engaging everything was.
The animal encounters are fantastic — we saw elephants, giraffes, big cats, kangaroos, and so many colourful birds and reptiles. My kids’ eyes lit up at every exhibit! The zoo exhibits are thoughtfully spaced, which makes exploring fun without feeling too crowded.
One of the biggest pluses for us was how pram-friendly and stroller accessible the pathways are. We easily navigated the whole zoo with our double pram, and there were plenty of shady rest spots and benches along the way.
The views of Sydney Harbour from the zoo are breathtaking and add a beautiful backdrop to the experience. We also enjoyed the keeper talks and feeding times, which were both educational and entertaining for the kids.
A couple of tips: • Take the sky safari cable car up/down — it’s fun and saves little legs from too much walking.
• Arrive early to avoid peak crowds and make the most of your day.
Overall, a highly recommended outing for families — especially with young kids. Definitely worth visiting when you’re in Sydney!Bhanu S — Google reviewHave a great day at the zoo I was there with a friend who is disabled so I got in without paying as a companion. I was amazed at how is had changed from the old days we only saw a portion of it but what we saw was excellent. A wonderful display of birds trained to fly free and exhibit the beauty of flight. Trained seals performing tricks on command providing great entertainment and enjoying it themselves. A lazy tiger asleep on the roof of a Jeep, preserving energy and avoiding the heat of the warm humid autumn day. Lunch at the shop there was commodious and prepared us for the rest of the afternoon. Ever a surprise as we passed by the turtles hard at play in a copulatory pose of ecstacy, the male turtle vomiting on the female as the climactic moment approached.
Lovely views over the water and the Queen Mary ship moored in front added to the momentous ness of the occasion.SAM D — Google review4.5(34945)•4.2(7769)Bradleys Head Rd, Mosman NSW 2088, Australia
Mentioned on BeachNature & ParksBondi Beach is a renowned destination that perfectly blends sun, surf, and style. This iconic stretch of sand attracts visitors from all over the globe with its stunning views and vibrant atmosphere. The beach is lined with trendy eateries where you can indulge in everything from refreshing kale smoothies to hearty breakfast bowls while soaking up the local vibe. For those looking for a bit of adventure, Bondi also boasts a skate park that adds to its lively charm.The Undisputed King: Iconic Bondi Beach
"Bondi Beach is more than just Sydney's most popular tourist beach—it's the heartbeat of Australian beach culture, all conveniently located just a stone's throw from the city!
The golden, sweeping sand and the electric-blue waves are absolutely postcard-perfect. It's the one beach in Sydney where you can instantly feel the energy: the surfers carving up the waves, the famous yellow and red of the 'Bondi Rescue' lifeguards on patrol, and the buzzing crowd that makes you feel like you're right where the action is.
What makes it truly special is the incredible atmosphere. It’s the perfect blend of serious surf action, relaxed sunbathing, and world-class people-watching. You can grab a coffee from a trendy cafe right on the promenade, dive into the historic Icebergs pool , or just sit on the sand and soak up the unique, laid-back-but-lively vibe.
Since it's so close to the CBD (easily reached by a short bus trip), it’s the ultimate, accessible escape. If you're visiting Sydney and only have time for one beach, make it Bondi. It’s iconic for a reason—it’s an essential, exhilarating taste of the Australian coastal lifestyle. A guaranteed 5-star experience!"
