JOURNEY FOR JUSTICE
1ST ANNIVERSARY: Journey for Justice to show the immorality of the immigration policy
This December 2023 marks the first anniversary of the Journey for Justice / Peregrinaje por la Justicia organized by Witness at the Border. Dozens of human and migrant rights activists from around the country set off on their Journey for Justice on December 3, 2022, in Brownsville, Texas, and ended their trek in San Ysidro, California, on December 18, 2022. The caravan went along along the entire length 2000 of the US-Mexico border.
The Journey was to honor the lives of migrants and asylum seekers who have suffered and especially those who have died at the U.S.-Mexico border. Up to October 2022, there were a record of 856 deaths. The Journey also meant to highlight the need for just and humane immigration legislation.
Here we publish some of the many articles from Witness at the Border’s Journey for Justice. Please visit witnessattheborder.org for more information about Witness at the Border and the Journey for Justice.
We thank Nanzi Muro y Francisco Mendoza for the photos and videoclips taken of Journey for Justice. They are included in this special report.
El Tribuno del Pueblo and its sister publication the People’s Tribune partnered and participated in this journey. Our participation was made possible by donations from our readers and friends. Please donate to El Tribuno del Pueblo to continue this work of education and truth-telling that hopefully will lead to organization and action against human rights violations.
The border is a destructive force: Joshua Rubin of Witness at the Border
In this interview with the People’s Tribune recorded Dec. 4, 2022, in Uvalde, Texas, Joshua Rubin discusses the Journey for Justice that began on Dec. 3 in Brownsville, Texas. Rubin is the founder of Witness at the Border, which organized the Journey for Justice, a 2,200-mile pilgrimage along the US-Mexico border from Brownsville to San Ysidro, California, to document what is happening to migrants and refugees as the result of US immigration policy.
The People’s Tribune and El Tribuno del Pueblo are among the more than 40 partner organizations supporting and reporting on the Journey for Justice, which is scheduled to end Dec. 18 in California. (Interview conducted by Bob Lee, with video by Francisco Mendoza.) Visit Witness At The Border's Website for more info: www.witnessattheborder.org.
Marina Vazquez Remembers Tornillo Detention Center
Marina Vazquez discusses how it feels to be back in Tornillo where the largest detention camp for migrant children exited. It was supposed to be a temporary solution, but a one-month contract to operate the camp stretched to two months, then three, then into the holidays as its population swelled to 6,000.
The People’s Tribune and El Tribuno del Pueblo were among the more than 40 partner organizations supporting and reporting on the Journey for Justice. (Interview conducted by Laura Garcia from El Tribuno del Pueblo.
Journey for Justice Stopped in Uvalde, Texas
On May 24, 2022, a mass shooting occurred at Robb Elementary in Uvalde, Texas. Nineteen young students and two teachers were murdered that day while seventeen others were injured. In December 2022, el Tribuno del Pueblo and the People's Tribune met with some of the family members as the community continues to heal from this tragedy.
After Title 42: Border Enforcement Zone in San Ysidro, California
In May 2023, el Tribuno del Pueblo and the People's Tribune visited migrants at the open air corridor between San Ysidro and Tijuana. The corridor is under U.S. jurisdiction, meaning that Border Patrol has to meet certain requirements when it comes to ensuring the wellbeing of migrants. Pedro Rios from the American Friends Service Committee speaks on the conditions migrants face at the corridor and how the community has stepped up and where the U.S. has failed.
1st Anniversary: Journey for Justice to Show the Immorality of the immigration Policy

Good morning and welcome to the last few days of June! Doesn’t seem at all possible that July is less than a week away and the 4th of July weekend is coming up. As a teacher I always felt like Independence Day was the midway point of summer, then it was quickly cruising downhill to the beginning of school. We always had several days of inservice that fell mid July and then school starting was about 3 weeks after that. Of course, now it won’t matter, right? We will be attending Back Stage in New Orleans when school begins this year so surely I won’t get those “back to school blues” feelings like all the previous years!!!
Creating Real Red Potted Geraniums!
This week’s focus will be the Potted Geranium bundle. Chris did a wonder job introducing the bundle last week during our private group page and I’ve been using it to create my Stamp n Sip projects for July. I love how easy these dies and stamps work together. Occasionally we have such detailed and intricate dies that there is a learning curve to the assembly of the flowers (thinking peonies here!) but this set was simple to play with!
FB LINK to Today’s Live!
I shared this card on my FB LIVE this morning on my business page Flick Of The Rist. To view, simply click on the link below, and while you are there please follow me on Facebook so you receive notifications of future FB Lives, my classes and stamping events, and any promotions from Stampin’ Up.
Sending Good Thoughts With The July Paper Pumpkin Kit!
“Seas” the day and set sail with across the ocean the Sending Good Thoughts Paper Pumpkin Kit! With beautifully designed nautical imagery, a fun message in a bottle motif, and sentiments that are “shore” to please, this month’s kit is full of warmth and fun.
Each kit contains enough supplies to create 9 cards—3 each of 3 daring designs—and 9 coordinating envelopes. This month’s Paper Pumpkin kit will have your loved ones feeling sand-tastic!
This kit includes:
- Sending Good Thoughts Photopolymer Stamp Set
- Bermuda Bay Classic Stampin’ Spot®
- Printed dry-embossed card bases
- Printed envelopes
- Printed die cuts
- Mini glue dots
Card size: 4-1/4″ x 5-1/2″ (10.8 x 14 cm)
Coordinating Stampin’ Up! colors: Balmy Blue, Basic Gray, Bermuda Bay, Fresh Freesia, Pacific Point, Poppy Parade
CLICK on the LINK below to sign up for this month’s kit! Each month there is an element of surprise!
Here is hoping you have a wonderful day full of everything you enjoy doing! Enjoy sometime creating and playing with your crafting arsenal! Until next time, keep stamping, keep crafting, and God Bless!

If you’re looking to spruce up your bathroom with a touch of bohemian charm, you’re in the right spot! We’ve gathered 15 delightful boho bathroom ideas that focus on vibrant colors, earthy textures, and lots of personality. Get ready to transform your space into a cozy oasis that reflects your unique style.
Freestanding Bathtubs as Statement Pieces
Freestanding bathtubs are perfect for creating a focal point in a boho bathroom. Their unique shapes and sizes can add a touch of character to your space. In this image, the sleek white tub stands out beautifully against the soft, draped curtains.
The addition of candles floating in the water and lush greenery gives an inviting vibe. It’s all about creating a relaxing atmosphere where you can unwind after a long day. The wooden bath tray adds a rustic touch, making it practical for holding candles or a good book.
In a boho bathroom, the combination of natural materials and soft lighting can transform your bathing experience. Think about how you can incorporate similar elements to make your bathroom feel like a serene escape.
Indoor Plants for a Lush Atmosphere
Indoor plants can transform your bathroom into a serene escape, adding life and color to the space. They not only beautify but also improve air quality, making your self-care rituals even more enjoyable.
In the image, a collection of plants like ferns and snake plants creates a vibrant atmosphere. Their varying shapes and textures contribute to a lush feel, perfect for a boho bathroom. Consider placing taller plants like palms in corners, while smaller potted ones can sit on shelves or window sills.
Incorporating a macramé wall hanging also complements the earthy vibe. It ties in beautifully with the plants and adds a touch of artistry. Accessorizing your shelves with decorative pots and skincare products creates a harmonious look, combining utility with style.
Unique Mirrors for a Personal Touch
Mirrors are more than just functional items; they can be key pieces in a boho bathroom. The image showcases a collection of unique mirrors, each with its own character and charm. These mirrors create a layered look, adding depth and personality to the space.
The round mirror with intricate detailing stands out, drawing the eye with its vintage appeal. It’s a perfect example of how a single mirror can serve as a statement piece. The smaller mirrors in varied shapes add a playful touch, encouraging creativity in your decor choices.
Incorporating different sizes and styles allows you to express your individual taste. Consider mixing ornate frames with simpler designs for a balanced yet eclectic vibe. The arrangement in the image encourages a casual, relaxed feel, making the bathroom a welcoming retreat.
Don’t overlook the practical side of mirrors either! They reflect light and can make smaller spaces feel larger. This collection not only enhances aesthetic appeal but also serves as a clever way to brighten your bathroom.
Earthy Color Palette with Terracotta
Embracing earthy tones can transform your bathroom into a serene oasis. This beautiful space features rich terracotta that adds warmth and depth. The walls, painted in a deep earthy hue, create a cozy atmosphere that feels inviting and grounded.
The terracotta sink and bathtub seamlessly blend with the overall color scheme, highlighting the natural beauty of this palette. It’s a subtle yet striking choice that pairs well with patterned tiles, creating a dynamic visual contrast.
Wooden shelves add an organic touch, providing space for plants and decorative items. The greenery not only enhances the earthy vibe but also brings life to the room. The hanging light fixture, with its soft fringe, complements the terracotta beautifully, casting a warm glow that makes the bathroom feel even more intimate.
Macramé Wall Hangings for Artistic Flair
Macramé wall hangings are a fantastic way to add character to your bathroom. This art form brings warmth and texture to any space. The image shows a beautifully crafted piece, showcasing intricate knots and natural fibers that create a stunning focal point.
Hanging macramé not only enhances the aesthetic appeal but also ties in with the boho vibe. The soft tones of the wall hanging complement the earthy colors of the surrounding space. Placing it above a bathtub or near a window can draw the eye and create a sense of harmony.
Consider mixing different sizes and styles of macramé to create depth. Using various textures can also add layers of interest to your bathroom. Whether you choose a large statement piece or smaller accent hangings, this artistic touch can transform a plain wall into a lively and inviting atmosphere.
Natural Wood Accents for a Cozy Vibe
When you think of a cozy bathroom, natural wood accents might come to mind. This space perfectly captures that vibe with its warm wooden shelves and sink. The rich texture of the wood adds a touch of nature, making you feel right at home every day.
The floating shelves not only provide storage but also showcase beautiful plants and a framed picture. This little detail brings life to the bathroom, enhancing the boho aesthetic. It’s a great way to add greenery without taking up too much space.
The wooden sink, carved from a single piece of wood, is a striking centerpiece. Its natural shape and finish blend seamlessly with the surrounding decor, creating a harmonious look. This unique feature pairs wonderfully with the clean white tiles and simple fixtures, making the room feel both stylish and inviting.
Overall, incorporating wood accents transforms a bathroom into a cozy retreat. Whether you opt for shelves, a sink, or even decorative touches, natural wood can elevate your space and make it feel warm and welcoming.
Woven Baskets for Practical Storage
Woven baskets are a delightful addition to any boho bathroom. They offer not only style but also practicality. In the image, you can see a lovely arrangement of various woven baskets providing storage for essentials.
These baskets come in different sizes, shapes, and colors, which adds visual interest to the space. The earthy tones and natural textures harmonize beautifully with the overall bohemian vibe. You can use them to store towels, toiletries, or even as decorative plant holders.
Placing baskets under the sink or near the shower creates a tidy environment. It’s a simple way to keep items organized while enhancing the cozy feel of your bathroom. Plus, they are easy to move around if you need extra space.
Woven baskets also pair well with other boho elements like textured rugs and hanging plants. This creates a cohesive look that feels warm and inviting. So, if you’re looking to add both beauty and functionality to your bathroom, consider incorporating some woven baskets!
Vintage Rugs to Add Warmth
Vintage rugs can really transform a bathroom, giving it a cozy touch that feels inviting. In the image, you can see how a beautifully patterned rug complements the space. The warm colors and intricate design add a sense of charm, making the bathroom feel less sterile and more like a retreat.
The rugs shown are not just for decoration; they also offer comfort underfoot. Stepping out of a bath onto a soft rug is a delightful experience. Plus, vintage styles often feature durable materials, ensuring they last in a moisture-prone area.
Incorporating these rugs into your bathroom can also serve as a conversation starter. Friends and family may admire the unique patterns and colors, and you can share the story behind your find. Whether you prefer bold florals or subtle geometric designs, there’s a vintage rug to fit any theme.
By layering these rugs in front of the bathtub or sink, you can create a warm atmosphere that encourages relaxation. Adding some greenery or decorative pieces, like the lantern seen in the image, enhances the boho vibe. So, if you’re looking to warm up your bathroom, consider a vintage rug as your go-to accessory.
Layered Textiles for Comfort and Style
Layering textiles is a key aspect of creating a cozy and welcoming boho bathroom. In the image, we see a beautiful blend of various textures and patterns that enhance the space’s comfort. The soft pillows on the floor invite relaxation, making it a perfect spot to unwind after a long day.
The use of different fabrics, from flowing curtains to woven rugs, adds depth to the design. The neutral color palette keeps the look serene while still feeling lively. Natural materials, like cotton and linen, contribute to the earthy vibe often associated with bohemian decor.
The addition of greenery in the bathroom adds a fresh touch and complements the layered textiles perfectly. Plants not only bring life to the space but also work beautifully with the earthly tones present in the textiles. Mixing and matching throws, bath mats, and decorative towels can create a look that is both stylish and inviting.
Colorful Tiles for a Playful Look
When it comes to creating a boho bathroom, colorful tiles can make all the difference. The vibrant, circular tiles in this image are a perfect example of how playful design elements can bring a space to life. Each tile features a mix of blues, reds, oranges, and yellows, creating a cheerful and inviting atmosphere. These colors not only add visual interest but also make the bathroom feel warm and welcoming. Pairing such a bold tile with natural textures, like the woven light fixture and the rattan basket, enhances the bohemian vibe. The lovely rug on the floor complements the tiles beautifully, tying the whole look together. If you want to infuse your bathroom with personality, consider choosing colorful tiles that reflect your style and bring joy to your daily routine.
Artistic Lighting Fixtures to Enhance Ambiance
Lighting can truly transform a bathroom, adding both functionality and charm. In this boho-inspired space, artistic fixtures play a key role in creating a warm and inviting atmosphere. The unique light fixtures, resembling delicate flowers, bring a touch of nature indoors, perfectly complementing the greenery scattered throughout.
These lighting options do more than just brighten the room; they become focal points that enhance the overall decor. The soft, diffused glow creates a relaxing environment, ideal for those long baths at the end of the day. With the right fixtures, you can achieve a cozy vibe that makes your bathroom feel more like a personal retreat.
Consider how the shapes and materials of your light fixtures can reflect your personal style. Whether you lean towards rustic, modern, or eclectic designs, there’s a wide array of options to explore. Mixing different textures, like the natural wood and soft glass seen here, can add depth and interest to your space.
Handcrafted Accessories for Authenticity
When it comes to creating a boho bathroom, handcrafted accessories are essential for adding a touch of authenticity. The image beautifully showcases a blend of natural materials that evoke a warm and inviting atmosphere.
Notice the carefully arranged wooden trays that not only serve a functional purpose but also enhance the overall aesthetic. These trays are perfect for holding soap or other small items, keeping your space organized and stylish.
The sleek, hand-crafted containers add a modern twist while maintaining a rustic charm. Their unique shapes and textures create visual interest, making them great conversation starters.
Additionally, the soft lighting from the glass fixtures complements the earthy tones of the wood and ceramics. This combination helps in setting a calming ambiance, ideal for unwinding after a long day.
Incorporating these handcrafted accessories can elevate your bathroom decor, making it a space that reflects your personal style while also embracing the bohemian spirit.
Personalized Artwork to Reflect Style
Adding personalized artwork to your bathroom can really bring your space to life. In the image above, vibrant colors and abstract shapes create a lively atmosphere that perfectly complements the boho style.
The large piece of art makes a bold statement, drawing the eye and inviting creativity. It’s not just about decoration; it’s about expressing who you are. Consider choosing artwork that resonates with your interests or travels, like a painting inspired by a favorite destination.
Incorporating candles and decorative accents around the bathtub enhances the cozy vibe. It turns a simple bath into a relaxing retreat. When choosing your artwork, think about colors that harmonize with the overall bathroom design. This way, every element in the room feels connected and thoughtfully placed.
Rustic Elements for a Natural Feel
A boho bathroom shouts charm and warmth, especially when you incorporate rustic elements. The image captures a space that beautifully blends natural materials with cozy design, creating an inviting atmosphere.
Notice the wooden beams on the ceiling? They add character and a sense of connection to the outdoors. The soft, earthy tones of the walls give the room a grounded feel, making it a perfect retreat.
The stone shelving unit is another standout feature. It’s both functional and stylish, showcasing potted plants and candles. This touch of greenery brings life and freshness, contributing to that natural vibe you want in a boho bathroom.
Don’t overlook the circular basin on the wooden vanity. It combines elegance with rusticity, serving as a focal point in the space. The overall design encourages a relaxed, easy-going atmosphere, perfect for unwinding after a long day.
With the right mix of rustic elements, your bathroom can transform into a serene oasis that feels connected to nature. Embrace these ideas to create a space where you can truly relax and recharge.
Functional Yet Stylish Vanities
When it comes to creating a boho bathroom, the vanity can serve as both a focal point and a practical piece of furniture. This particular vanity features a warm wood finish that adds a touch of rustic charm.
The choice of materials is crucial. The combination of the wooden vanity with a sleek marble countertop creates a balanced look. The rich tones of the wood complement the soft, natural hues of the marble, giving the space a cozy yet sophisticated vibe.
Lighting is another important aspect. Here, industrial-style bulbs cast a warm glow on the exposed brick wall, enhancing the overall ambiance. The mix of textures—from the brick to the wood and marble—adds depth and interest.
Don’t forget the decorations! A few carefully chosen items like candles and a stylish plant can bring life to the vanity area. This not only makes it functional but also adds to the relaxed, inviting atmosphere typical of boho design.
Lastly, consider storage options. Open shelving and baskets provide a neat way to keep essentials organized while maintaining a casual look. It’s all about finding that perfect balance between style and practicality.
Open Shelving for Display and Storage
Open shelving can add a unique charm to your bathroom while offering practical storage solutions. The image beautifully illustrates how to achieve a boho vibe using shelves that display a mix of decorative and functional items.
In this setup, you can see a variety of pottery, candles, and even some greenery, which enhances the natural feel of a bohemian bathroom. The soft, muted colors of the shelves and wall create a serene backdrop for the eclectic items displayed.
The wooden ladder adds a rustic touch, providing a place to hang towels that are easily accessible. This combination of display and storage not only keeps the space organized but also adds personality and warmth.
Consider using baskets or decorative boxes on your open shelves to store smaller items while still showcasing some unique decor pieces. Mixing textures like ceramic, wood, and textiles can create a cozy yet stylish ambiance.
❓ Boho Bathroom FAQ
Which plants actually thrive in a bathroom?
Try ferns, pothos, ZZ, snake plant, and peace lily. They tolerate humidity and lower light—perfect for that lush boho vibe.
Can I use vintage rugs in a bathroom?
Yes—choose wool or performance blends, use a non-slip pad, and hang to dry after steamy showers to extend life.
How do I protect wood accents from moisture?
Seal with a water-resistant finish (e.g., marine-grade varnish or penetrating oil), avoid direct splash zones, and allow good ventilation.
What’s an easy way to get the look on a budget?
Layer a tray + basket storage, add a macramé piece and one statement mirror, then bring in a couple of plants for instant warmth.

